{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke4Wb9ALnEgr6VttYt4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JBDxND6C62P1DNVCqa1wwW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7744,"cache_read_input_tokens":55541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7744},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"6754a9ca-2337-4d73-8a7a-183a9c49029b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:27.577Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke4WJGTHX6g5dXkGtjL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JBDxND6C62P1DNVCqa1wwW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBDxND6C62P1DNVCqa1wwW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n2\t\n3\tAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\n4\tplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\n5\tround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\n6\tscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\n7\tround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n8\t\n9\t**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n10\t\n11\tThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\n12\tdescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n13\t\n14\t- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n15\t- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n16\t\n17\tTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n18\t\n19\t> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n20\t> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n21\t> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## Modes\n26\t\n27\tA game declares one mode.\n28\t\n29\t| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n30\t|---|---|---|\n31\t| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n32\t| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n33\t| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n34\t\n35\t- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n36\t  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n37\t- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n38\t  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n39\t  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n40\t- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n41\t  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n42\t  world the host sends them.\n43\t\n44\tGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n45\t`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## A round\n50\t\n51\t1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n52\t   to 30 seconds with the game's card, longer if one asks for more time: what\n53\t   the game is, how to win, the controls. The card is the hub's, from the\n54\t   game's tags, or the game's own (*The card*).\n55\t2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n56\t3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n57\t4. The game reports how it goes.\n58\t5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n59\t   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n60\t   over the game, then removes it.\n61\t\n62\t### Tags\n63\t\n64\tIn the game's `<head>`:\n65\t\n66\t```html\n67\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n68\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n69\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n70\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n71\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n75\t  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n76\t  is in that range.\n77\t- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n78\t- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n79\t  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n80\t\n81\tOptional:\n82\t\n83\t- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n84\t  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n85\t- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n86\t  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n87\t\n88\t### The client\n89\t\n90\t[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\n91\tis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\n92\tafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n93\t\n94\t- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n95\t  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n96\t- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n97\t  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n98\t  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n99\t- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n100\t  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n101\t  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n102\t\n103\tThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\n104\tedited copy is not replaced.\n105\t\n106\t### Joining\n107\t\n108\t- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n109\t- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n110\t  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n111\t- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n112\t  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n113\t  the game runs as it does on its own.\n114\t- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n115\t  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n116\t- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n117\t  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n118\t  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n119\t\n120\t`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n121\t\n122\t| Field | |\n123\t|---|---|\n124\t| `me` | this copy's player id |\n125\t| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n126\t| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n127\t| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n128\t| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n129\t| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n130\t\n131\tNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\n132\tfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n133\t\n134\t### The card\n135\t\n136\tBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\n137\tnext and say when they are ready. A player can ask for more time, which adds\n138\tten seconds; while more than half of them are asking, the countdown holds.\n139\tBy default the hub shows its own card over the game. A game can make the\n140\tcard its own, as part of the game:\n141\t\n142\t```js\n143\tAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n144\t```\n145\t\n146\tThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\n147\tscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\n148\ttitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\n149\tit deserves.\n150\t\n151\tWhile it is on, the card shows:\n152\t\n153\t- the game's name;\n154\t- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n155\t- how to win the round;\n156\t- the controls this player will use;\n157\t- the time left, from the `card` event.\n158\t\n159\tAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\n160\ton the card:\n161\t\n162\t- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n163\t  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n164\t- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n165\t  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n166\t\n167\tNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\n168\tchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\n169\tnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n170\t`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n171\t\n172\t`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n173\t\n174\t| Field | |\n175\t|---|---|\n176\t| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n177\t| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n178\t| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n179\t| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n180\t| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n181\t| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n182\t\n183\t### The start\n184\t\n185\t`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n186\t`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\n187\tgive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n188\t`start`.\n189\t\n190\t### Reporting\n191\t\n192\t- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n193\t  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n194\t  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n195\t- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n196\t  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n197\t  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n198\t- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n199\t  by the host only:\n200\t  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n201\t    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n202\t    placed last.\n203\t  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n204\t  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n205\t\n206\t### Time-up and the end\n207\t\n208\t- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n209\t  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n210\t  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n211\t  `finish()` by then is void.\n212\t- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n213\t  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n214\t  game, then removes it.\n215\t\n216\t| `end` reason | |\n217\t|---|---|\n218\t| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n219\t| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n220\t| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n221\t| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n222\t| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n223\t\n224\t### Leaving\n225\t\n226\t- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n227\t  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n228\t- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n229\t- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n230\t  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n231\t- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n232\t  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n233\t  that player leaving.\n234\t\n235\t### Scoring\n236\t\n237\t- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n238\t  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n239\t  progress.\n240\t- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n241\t  result instead of medals.\n242\t- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n243\t\n244\t`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\n245\tresults:\n246\t\n247\t- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n248\t  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n249\t- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n250\t  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n251\t\n252\tPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n253\t\n254\t---\n255\t\n256\t## Sending data between copies\n257\t\n258\t### Parallel\n259\t\n260\tThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n261\t\n262\t### Ghost\n263\t\n264\tEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\n265\tthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\n266\tonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\n267\tcharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n268\t\n269\t### Shared world\n270\t\n271\t- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n272\t  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n273\t- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n274\t  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n275\t  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n276\t- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n277\t  every copy.\n278\t\n279\t### `send()` and `message`\n280\t\n281\t- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n282\t  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n283\t- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n284\t  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n285\t  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n286\t- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n287\t- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n288\t  client drops the rest.\n289\t- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n290\t  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n291\t  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n292\t  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n293\t\n294\t---\n295\t\n296\t## Rules\n297\t\n298\tIn a session:\n299\t\n300\t- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n301\t  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n302\t- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n303\t  names. Names come from the hub.\n304\t- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n305\t  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n306\t  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n307\t- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n308\t  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n309\t  is held.\n310\t\n311\tEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\n312\tone, the game is not affected.\n313\t\n314\t---\n315\t\n316\t## Test it\n317\t\n318\tThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\n319\tand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\n320\tto the game:\n321\t\n322\t```bash\n323\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n324\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\n325\tcurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\n326\tpython3 -m http.server 8000\n327\t```\n328\t\n329\tThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\n330\tThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n331\t`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n332\t`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n333\t`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n334\t\n335\tThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n336\t`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n337\t`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n338\t\n339\t- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n340\t- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n341\t- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n342\t  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n343\t- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n344\t  player of its own;\n345\t- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n346\t  told the round ended;\n347\t- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n348\t\n349\t**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\n350\tcases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n351\t`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\n352\tgame is served from the harness's own origin.\n353\t\n354\tIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\n355\tchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\n356\truns there.\n357\t\n358\t---\n359\t\n360\t## Reference\n361\t\n362\t### Tags\n363\t\n364\t| Tag | |\n365\t|---|---|\n366\t| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n367\t| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n368\t| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n369\t| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n370\t| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n371\t| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n372\t| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n373\t\n374\t### API\n375\t\n376\t| | |\n377\t|---|---|\n378\t| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n379\t| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n380\t| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n381\t| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n382\t| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n383\t| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n384\t| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n385\t| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n386\t| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n387\t| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n388\t| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n389\t| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n390\t| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n391\t\n392\t`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\n393\tread them.\n394\t\n395\t| Event | Arguments |\n396\t|---|---|\n397\t| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n398\t| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n399\t| `message` | `data, from` |\n400\t| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n401\t| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n402\t| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n403\t\n404\tEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\n405\torder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\n406\treach the game through the client unchanged.\n407\t\n408\t### Versions\n409\t\n410\tThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\n411\tgames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\n412\tprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n413\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"4bf277b0-d2ab-4e31-8f93-7bce9092740e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:27.582Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/README.md","content":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card, longer if one asks for more time: what\n   the game is, how to win, the controls. The card is the hub's, from the\n   game's tags, or the game's own (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. A player can ask for more time, which adds\nten seconds; while more than half of them are asking, the countdown holds.\nBy default the hub shows its own card over the game. A game can make the\ncard its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n","numLines":413,"startLine":1,"totalLines":413}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JBDxND6C62P1DNVCqa1wwW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke4Wb9ALnEgr6VttYt4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019rr5GfjtrE8zMp6kgoQBGC","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/retrofit.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7744,"cache_read_input_tokens":55541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7744},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"6f4de586-e9c0-4da9-ae60-84b7386aa0c3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:28.235Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke4WJGTHX6g5dXkGtjL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019rr5GfjtrE8zMp6kgoQBGC":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/retrofit.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rr5GfjtrE8zMp6kgoQBGC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n2\t\n3\tThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\n4\tstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\n5\tpage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\n6\tis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n7\t[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\n8\tfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\n9\tand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\tYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\n14\tin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\n15\ttime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\n16\thow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\n17\taudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n18\t\n19\tA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n20\t`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\n21\tthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\n22\tagainst it:\n23\t\n24\t<protocol>\n25\t{{contract}}\n26\t</protocol>\n27\t\n28\tDo only this:\n29\t\n30\t1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n31\t   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n32\t2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n33\t   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n34\t   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n35\t   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n36\t   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n37\t   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n38\t3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n39\t   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n40\t   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n41\t   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n42\t   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n43\t4. Whenever the score changes, call\n44\t   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n45\t   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n46\t5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n47\t   `AIHub.result({ time, stats })` or `AIHub.result({ score, stats })` once.\n48\t   `stats` holds up to six numbers the game already keeps that say how the\n49\t   run went, each under a name of at most 16 characters, for example\n50\t   `{ Coins: 42, 'Best combo': 7 }`; add no counting for it, and leave it out\n51\t   if the game keeps none. In `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current\n52\t   score and stats at once if the run is still going.\n53\t6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n54\t7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n55\t   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n56\t   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n57\t   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n58\t8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n59\t\n60\tDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\n61\ttouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\n62\tthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\n63\tthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\n64\tlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\n65\tgame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\n66\teither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\n67\tdescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n68\t\n69\tIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\n70\tline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n71\t\n72\tOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\n73\tyou changed.\n74\t\n75\t{{notes}}\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"1fbf3aa1-94dc-4a7a-859d-30c6678b6a78","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:28.240Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/retrofit.md","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time, stats })` or `AIHub.result({ score, stats })` once.\n   `stats` holds up to six numbers the game already keeps that say how the\n   run went, each under a name of at most 16 characters, for example\n   `{ Coins: 42, 'Best combo': 7 }`; add no counting for it, and leave it out\n   if the game keeps none. In `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current\n   score and stats at once if the run is still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019rr5GfjtrE8zMp6kgoQBGC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke4Wb9ALnEgr6VttYt4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0164eF4y6uyuoDDbK2A5hDfh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/round.js"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7744,"cache_read_input_tokens":55541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7744},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"11518437-57bb-4a16-ab10-48e3cc6b32d1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:28.876Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke4WJGTHX6g5dXkGtjL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0164eF4y6uyuoDDbK2A5hDfh":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/round.js"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0164eF4y6uyuoDDbK2A5hDfh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n3\t * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n4\t *\n5\t * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n6\t * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n7\t * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n8\t * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n9\t * without waiting for one.\n10\t *\n11\t * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n12\t * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n13\t */\n14\t\n15\texport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n16\t  helloMs: 10_000,\n17\t  readyMs: 45_000,\n18\t  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n19\t  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n20\t  countdownMs: 3_000,\n21\t  graceMs: 5_000,\n22\t  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n23\t  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n24\t});\n25\t\n26\t/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\n27\texport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n28\t\n29\texport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n30\t\n31\t/** Each mode's name on screen. */\n32\texport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n33\t\n34\t/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\n35\tconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n36\t\n37\t/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\n38\texport function modeOf(word) {\n39\t  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n40\t  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n41\t}\n42\t\n43\t/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\n44\texport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n45\t\n46\t/**\n47\t * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n48\t * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n49\t * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n50\t * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n51\t */\n52\texport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n53\t\n54\tconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n55\t  now: () => Date.now(),\n56\t  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n57\t  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n58\t};\n59\t\n60\t/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\n61\texport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n62\t  const typical = Number(minutes);\n63\t  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n64\t  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n65\t}\n66\t\n67\t/**\n68\t * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n69\t * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n70\t * place.\n71\t */\n72\texport function rankResults(results, ids) {\n73\t  const timed = [];\n74\t  const scored = [];\n75\t  const silent = [];\n76\t  for (const id of ids) {\n77\t    const r = results.get(id);\n78\t    if (r && Number.isFinite(r.time)) timed.push([id, r.time]);\n79\t    else if (r && Number.isFinite(r.score)) scored.push([id, r.score]);\n80\t    else silent.push(id);\n81\t  }\n82\t  const groups = (list, order) => {\n83\t    list.sort((a, b) => order * (a[1] - b[1]) || a[0] - b[0]);\n84\t    const out = [];\n85\t    for (const [id, value] of list) {\n86\t      const last = out[out.length - 1];\n87\t      if (last && last.value === value) last.ids.push(id);\n88\t      else out.push({ value, ids: [id] });\n89\t    }\n90\t    return out.map((g) => g.ids);\n91\t  };\n92\t  return [...groups(timed, 1), ...groups(scored, -1), ...(silent.length ? [silent] : [])];\n93\t}\n94\t\n95\t/** A time or score as a number: finite, given as a number or as text; NaN for null, '' or true, which Number() would make 0. */\n96\tconst asNumber = (v) => (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '') ? Number(v) : NaN);\n97\t\n98\t/** How much of a round's highlights the results card shows: a game cannot flood it. */\n99\texport const HIGHLIGHTS = Object.freeze({ stats: 6, statName: 16, statText: 16, awards: 3, title: 24, detail: 40 });\n100\t\n101\t/** One player's stats, trimmed: up to six names, each a finite number or a short text. Null when none survive. */\n102\texport function cleanStats(stats) {\n103\t  if (!stats || typeof stats !== 'object' || Array.isArray(stats)) return null;\n104\t  const out = {};\n105\t  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(stats).slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.stats)) {\n106\t    const label = String(name).trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statName);\n107\t    if (!label) continue;\n108\t    if (typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value)) out[label] = value;\n109\t    else if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim()) out[label] = value.trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statText);\n110\t  }\n111\t  return Object.keys(out).length ? out : null;\n112\t}\n113\t\n114\t/**\n115\t * Awards, trimmed: `{ id, title, detail? }`, at most three a player, for\n116\t * players of this round. A result's awards are about its own player: `self` is its id.\n117\t */\n118\texport function cleanAwards(awards, ids, self = null) {\n119\t  if (!Array.isArray(awards)) return [];\n120\t  const given = new Map();\n121\t  const out = [];\n122\t  for (const a of awards) {\n123\t    const id = self ?? a?.id;\n124\t    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\n125\t    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\n126\t    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\n127\t    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\n128\t    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\n129\t  }\n130\t  return out;\n131\t}\n132\t\n133\t/**\n134\t * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\n135\t * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\n136\t * left out lands in a last group of their own.\n137\t */\n138\texport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\n139\t  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\n140\t  const all = new Set(allIds);\n141\t  const seen = new Set();\n142\t  const groups = [];\n143\t  for (const group of standings) {\n144\t    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\n145\t    const kept = [];\n146\t    for (const id of ids) {\n147\t      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\n148\t      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\n149\t      seen.add(id);\n150\t      kept.push(id);\n151\t    }\n152\t    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\n153\t  }\n154\t  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n155\t  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\n156\t  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n157\t  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\n158\t  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\n159\t}\n160\t\n161\t/**\n162\t * @param {object} o\n163\t * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\n164\t * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\n165\t * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\n166\t * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\n167\t *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\n168\t *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\n169\t * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\n170\t * @param {number} o.seed\n171\t * @param {number} o.limitMs\n172\t * @param {{now:()=>number, setTimeout:Function, clearTimeout:Function}} [o.clock]\n173\t * @param {(key:string, msg:object) => void} o.deliver\n174\t * @param {(status:object) => void} [o.onStatus]\n175\t * @param {(record:object) => void} [o.onEnd]\n176\t * @param {boolean} [o.gate]          the hub shows a splash and collects the players' ready itself:\n177\t *                                    games ready up once loaded, and the round starts on release()\n178\t */\n179\texport function createRound({\n180\t  round,\n181\t  players,\n182\t  hostKey,\n183\t  mode = null,\n184\t  seed,\n185\t  limitMs,\n186\t  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\n187\t  deliver,\n188\t  onStatus = () => {},\n189\t  onEnd = () => {},\n190\t  timings = TIMINGS,\n191\t  gate = false,\n192\t  serverKey = null,\n193\t}) {\n194\t  mode = modeOf(mode);\n195\t  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\n196\t  const seats = [...players]\n197\t    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\n198\t    .map((p, id) => ({\n199\t      id,\n200\t      key: p.key,\n201\t      slot: p.slot,\n202\t      name: p.name,\n203\t      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\n204\t      hello: false,\n205\t      ready: false,\n206\t      out: null,\n207\t      result: null,\n208\t      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\n209\t      progress: null,\n210\t      stats: null,\n211\t      awards: [],\n212\t      caps: null,\n213\t      hidden: null,\n214\t    }));\n215\t  const server = serverKey\n216\t    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\n217\t    : null;\n218\t  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\n219\t  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\n220\t  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\n221\t  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\n222\t  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\n223\t  const timers = new Set();\n224\t  const issues = [];\n225\t  let phase = 'loading';\n226\t  let goAt = null;\n227\t  let record = null;\n228\t  let released = !gate;\n229\t\n230\t  const later = (ms, fn) => {\n231\t    const handle = clock.setTimeout(() => {\n232\t      timers.delete(handle);\n233\t      fn();\n234\t    }, Math.max(0, ms));\n235\t    timers.add(handle);\n236\t    return handle;\n237\t  };\n238\t  const cancel = (handle) => {\n239\t    if (handle == null) return;\n240\t    clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n241\t    timers.delete(handle);\n242\t  };\n243\t\n244\t  /** The players still in the round. */\n245\t  const present = () => seats.filter((s) => !s.out);\n246\t  /** The copies still in the round: the players, and the server. */\n247\t  const presentCopies = () => copies.filter((s) => !s.out);\n248\t  const selfReported = () => SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n249\t  const needsHost = () => !selfReported();\n250\t  const send = (seat, msg) => deliver(seat.key, { round, ...msg });\n251\t  const toPresent = (msg, except = null) => {\n252\t    for (const s of presentCopies()) if (s !== except && s.hello) send(s, msg);\n253\t  };\n254\t  const issue = (seat, problem) => {\n255\t    issues.push({ key: seat?.key ?? null, id: seat?.id ?? null, problem });\n256\t    status();\n257\t  };\n258\t\n259\t  function status() {\n260\t    onStatus({\n261\t      round,\n262\t      phase,\n263\t      mode,\n264\t      host: host.id,\n265\t      goAt,\n266\t      gate,\n267\t      released,\n268\t      players: seats.map((s) => ({\n269\t        id: s.id,\n270\t        key: s.key,\n271\t        slot: s.slot,\n272\t        name: s.name,\n273\t        color: s.color,\n274\t        hello: s.hello,\n275\t        ready: s.ready,\n276\t        out: s.out,\n277\t        result: s.result,\n278\t        client: s.caps?.client ?? null,\n279\t      })),\n280\t      server: server && { id: server.id, key: server.key, hello: server.hello, ready: server.ready, out: server.out, client: server.caps?.client ?? null },\n281\t      issues: issues.slice(),\n282\t    });\n283\t  }\n284\t\n285\t  function welcome(seat) {\n286\t    send(seat, {\n287\t      type: 'welcome',\n288\t      me: seat.id,\n289\t      host: host.id,\n290\t      players: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, name: s.name, color: s.color })),\n291\t      keys: copies.map((s) => s.key),\n292\t      mode,\n293\t      seed: seed >>> 0,\n294\t      limitMs,\n295\t      ...(gate ? { splash: true } : {}),\n296\t      ...(seat === server ? { server: true } : {}),\n297\t    });\n298\t    for (const s of seats) if (s.out) send(seat, { type: 'leave', id: s.id, reason: s.out });\n299\t  }\n300\t\n301\t  function markOut(seat, reason) {\n302\t    if (seat.out || phase === 'ended') return;\n303\t    seat.out = reason;\n304\t    cancel(seat.hidden);\n305\t    seat.hidden = null;\n306\t    toPresent({ type: 'leave', id: seat.id, reason });\n307\t    // A player who sat out is still at the hub: tell their game it is over for them.\n308\t    if (reason === 'not-ready' && seat.hello) send(seat, { type: 'end', reason: 'sat-out' });\n309\t  }\n310\t\n311\t  function settle() {\n312\t    if (phase === 'ended') return;\n313\t    const left = present();\n314\t    if (!left.length) return finishVoid('no-players');\n315\t    if (needsHost() && host.out) {\n316\t      return finishVoid(host.out === 'not-ready' ? 'host-not-ready' : 'host-left', phase === 'loading' ? 'void' : 'host-left');\n317\t    }\n318\t    if (phase === 'loading') {\n319\t      if (released && presentCopies().every((s) => s.ready)) begin();\n320\t      return;\n321\t    }\n322\t    if (selfReported() && left.every((s) => s.result)) finishResults();\n323\t  }\n324\t\n325\t  function begin() {\n326\t    phase = 'countdown';\n327\t    goAt = clock.now() + t.countdownMs;\n328\t    toPresent({ type: 'start', at: goAt });\n329\t    later(t.countdownMs, () => {\n330\t      if (phase === 'countdown') {\n331\t        phase = 'playing';\n332\t        status();\n333\t      }\n334\t    });\n335\t    later(t.countdownMs + limitMs, timeUp);\n336\t    status();\n337\t  }\n338\t\n339\t  function timeUp() {\n340\t    if (phase === 'ended' || phase === 'grace') return;\n341\t    phase = 'grace';\n342\t    toPresent({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: t.graceMs });\n343\t    later(t.graceMs, () => {\n344\t      if (phase === 'ended') return;\n345\t      if (selfReported()) finishResults();\n346\t      else finishVoid('no-result');\n347\t    });\n348\t    status();\n349\t  }\n350\t\n351\t  function finishResults() {\n352\t    // A player still here who never reported is ranked by the last progress the hub saw from them.\n353\t    const results = new Map(\n354\t      seats.filter((s) => s.result || (!s.out && Number.isFinite(s.progress))).map((s) => [s.id, s.result ?? { score: s.progress, fallback: true }])\n355\t    );\n356\t    // Whoever reported and then left keeps their place: only those who left with nothing count as beaten.\n357\t    const ranked = rankResults(results, seats.filter((s) => !s.out || s.result).map((s) => s.id));\n358\t    const gone = seats.filter((s) => s.out && !s.result).map((s) => s.id);\n359\t    const scores = {};\n360\t    for (const [id, r] of results) scores[id] = Number.isFinite(r.time) ? r.time : r.score;\n361\t    const stats = Object.fromEntries(seats.filter((s) => s.stats).map((s) => [s.id, s.stats]));\n362\t    const awards = seats.flatMap((s) => s.awards);\n363\t    finishPlayed(gone.length ? [...ranked, gone] : ranked, { scores, results: Object.fromEntries(results), stats, awards });\n364\t  }\n365\t\n366\t  function finishPlayed(standings, extra = {}) {\n367\t    end({ status: 'played', reason: 'finished', endReason: 'finished', standings, ...extra });\n368\t  }\n369\t\n370\t  function finishVoid(reason, endReason = 'void') {\n371\t    end({ status: 'void', reason, endReason, standings: null });\n372\t  }\n373\t\n374\t  function end(outcome) {\n375\t    if (phase === 'ended') return;\n376\t    phase = 'ended';\n377\t    for (const handle of timers) clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n378\t    timers.clear();\n379\t    const msg = { type: 'end', reason: outcome.endReason };\n380\t    if (outcome.standings) msg.standings = outcome.standings;\n381\t    toPresent(msg);\n382\t    record = {\n383\t      round,\n384\t      mode,\n385\t      hostId: host.id,\n386\t      ...outcome,\n387\t      players: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, key: s.key, slot: s.slot, name: s.name, color: s.color, out: s.out })),\n388\t      issues: issues.slice(),\n389\t    };\n390\t    status();\n391\t    onEnd(record);\n392\t  }\n393\t\n394\t  function receive(key, msg) {\n395\t    const seat = byKey.get(key);\n396\t    if (!seat || !msg || typeof msg.type !== 'string' || phase === 'ended' || seat.out) return;\n397\t    switch (msg.type) {\n398\t      case 'hello': {\n399\t        if (seat.hello) return;\n400\t        seat.hello = true;\n401\t        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\n402\t        if (msg.v !== 1) issue(seat, `hello speaks protocol ${JSON.stringify(msg.v)}, not 1`);\n403\t        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\n404\t        if (!mode && said) mode = said;\n405\t        else if (msg.mode && said !== mode) issue(seat, `hello says mode ${msg.mode}, the round is ${mode}`);\n406\t        welcome(seat);\n407\t        status();\n408\t        return;\n409\t      }\n410\t      case 'ready':\n411\t        if (!seat.hello || seat.ready || phase !== 'loading') return;\n412\t        seat.ready = true;\n413\t        status();\n414\t        return settle();\n415\t      case 'result': {\n416\t        if (!selfReported()) return issue(seat, `result is for parallel and ghost; this round is ${mode}`);\n417\t        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'result before start');\n418\t        if (seat.result) return;\n419\t        const time = asNumber(msg.time);\n420\t        const score = asNumber(msg.score);\n421\t        if (Number.isFinite(time)) seat.result = { time };\n422\t        else if (Number.isFinite(score)) seat.result = { score };\n423\t        else return issue(seat, 'result needs a finite time or score');\n424\t        seat.stats = cleanStats(msg.stats);\n425\t        seat.awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids, seat.id);\n426\t        status();\n427\t        return settle();\n428\t      }\n429\t      case 'finish': {\n430\t        if (selfReported()) return issue(seat, `finish is for a shared world; ${mode} games report result`);\n431\t        if (seat !== host) return issue(seat, 'finish from a player who is not the host');\n432\t        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'finish before start');\n433\t        const checked = checkStandings(msg.standings, present().map((s) => s.id), ids);\n434\t        if (!checked.ok) return issue(seat, `finish ignored: ${checked.problem}`);\n435\t        const scores = msg.scores && typeof msg.scores === 'object' ? msg.scores : undefined;\n436\t        const given = msg.stats && typeof msg.stats === 'object' ? msg.stats : {};\n437\t        const stats = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, cleanStats(given[id])]).filter(([, v]) => v));\n438\t        const awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids);\n439\t        // won makes it a team result; a game tagged co-op that leaves it out lost, as co-op always read it.\n440\t        const won = typeof msg.won === 'boolean' ? msg.won : seat.caps?.mode === 'co-op' ? false : undefined;\n441\t        return finishPlayed(checked.standings, { scores, won, stats, awards });\n442\t      }\n443\t      case 'error':\n444\t        issue(seat, `game error: ${String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 200)}`);\n445\t        if (msg.fatal) {\n446\t          if (needsHost() && seat === host) return finishVoid('host-error');\n447\t          markOut(seat, 'disconnected');\n448\t          status();\n449\t          settle();\n450\t        }\n451\t        return;\n452\t      case 'vis':\n453\t        if (seat !== host || !needsHost()) return;\n454\t        if (msg.hidden && seat.hidden == null && phase !== 'loading') {\n455\t          seat.hidden = later(t.hiddenMs, () => finishVoid('host-hidden'));\n456\t        } else if (!msg.hidden) {\n457\t          cancel(seat.hidden);\n458\t          seat.hidden = null;\n459\t        }\n460\t        return;\n461\t      default:\n462\t        return issue(seat, `unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);\n463\t    }\n464\t  }\n465\t\n466\t  function leave(key, reason = 'left') {\n467\t    const seat = byKey.get(key);\n468\t    if (!seat || seat.out || phase === 'ended') return;\n469\t    markOut(seat, reason);\n470\t    status();\n471\t    settle();\n472\t  }\n473\t\n474\t  const sitOut = (test) => () => {\n475\t    if (phase !== 'loading') return;\n476\t    for (const s of copies) if (test(s) && !s.out) markOut(s, 'not-ready');\n477\t    status();\n478\t    settle();\n479\t  };\n480\t\n481\t  function startRound() {\n482\t    // A gated round waits on the hub's splash, however long it holds: only\n483\t    // release() starts the clock on the games that are still loading.\n484\t    if (!gate) {\n485\t      later(t.helloMs, sitOut((s) => !s.hello));\n486\t      later(t.readyMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\n487\t    }\n488\t    status();\n489\t  }\n490\t\n491\t  /** The splash is over: start as soon as every game has loaded, and wait loadGraceMs at most for the slow ones. */\n492\t  function release() {\n493\t    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\n494\t    released = true;\n495\t    later(t.loadGraceMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\n496\t    status();\n497\t    settle();\n498\t  }\n499\t\n500\t  startRound();\n501\t\n502\t  return {\n503\t    receive,\n504\t    leave,\n505\t    release,\n506\t    /** Call time now, as the cap would: the host pressed \"End round\". */\n507\t    timeUp() {\n508\t      if (phase === 'countdown' || phase === 'playing') timeUp();\n509\t    },\n510\t    /** A player's progress score, as the hub's scoreboard saw it (parallel and ghost). */\n511\t    progress(id, score) {\n512\t      const seat = seats[id];\n513\t      if (seat && !seat.out && !seat.result && Number.isFinite(score) && phase !== 'ended') seat.progress = score;\n514\t    },\n515\t    /** End the round now: the session ended, or the host skipped this game. */\n516\t    abort(reason = 'skipped') {\n517\t      finishVoid(reason, reason === 'session-ended' ? 'session-ended' : 'void');\n518\t    },\n519\t    get phase() {\n520\t      return phase;\n521\t    },\n522\t    get released() {\n523\t      return released;\n524\t    },\n525\t    get record() {\n526\t      return record;\n527\t    },\n528\t    get mode() {\n529\t      return mode;\n530\t    },\n531\t    seats: () => seats.map((s) => ({ ...s, hidden: undefined })),\n532\t  };\n533\t}\n534\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"48d64d6d-820e-44ea-b0f7-8affd505c393","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:28.881Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/hub/round.js","content":"/**\n * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\nexport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n  helloMs: 10_000,\n  readyMs: 45_000,\n  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n  countdownMs: 3_000,\n  graceMs: 5_000,\n  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n});\n\n/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\nexport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n\nexport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n\n/** Each mode's name on screen. */\nexport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n\n/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\nconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n\n/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\nexport function modeOf(word) {\n  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n}\n\n/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\nexport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n\n/**\n * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n */\nexport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n\nconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n  now: () => Date.now(),\n  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n};\n\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\nexport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n  const typical = Number(minutes);\n  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n}\n\n/**\n * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n * place.\n */\nexport function rankResults(results, ids) {\n  const timed = [];\n  const scored = [];\n  const silent = [];\n  for (const id of ids) {\n    const r = results.get(id);\n    if (r && Number.isFinite(r.time)) timed.push([id, r.time]);\n    else if (r && Number.isFinite(r.score)) scored.push([id, r.score]);\n    else silent.push(id);\n  }\n  const groups = (list, order) => {\n    list.sort((a, b) => order * (a[1] - b[1]) || a[0] - b[0]);\n    const out = [];\n    for (const [id, value] of list) {\n      const last = out[out.length - 1];\n      if (last && last.value === value) last.ids.push(id);\n      else out.push({ value, ids: [id] });\n    }\n    return out.map((g) => g.ids);\n  };\n  return [...groups(timed, 1), ...groups(scored, -1), ...(silent.length ? [silent] : [])];\n}\n\n/** A time or score as a number: finite, given as a number or as text; NaN for null, '' or true, which Number() would make 0. */\nconst asNumber = (v) => (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '') ? Number(v) : NaN);\n\n/** How much of a round's highlights the results card shows: a game cannot flood it. */\nexport const HIGHLIGHTS = Object.freeze({ stats: 6, statName: 16, statText: 16, awards: 3, title: 24, detail: 40 });\n\n/** One player's stats, trimmed: up to six names, each a finite number or a short text. Null when none survive. */\nexport function cleanStats(stats) {\n  if (!stats || typeof stats !== 'object' || Array.isArray(stats)) return null;\n  const out = {};\n  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(stats).slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.stats)) {\n    const label = String(name).trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statName);\n    if (!label) continue;\n    if (typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value)) out[label] = value;\n    else if (typeof value === 'string' && value.trim()) out[label] = value.trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.statText);\n  }\n  return Object.keys(out).length ? out : null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Awards, trimmed: `{ id, title, detail? }`, at most three a player, for\n * players of this round. A result's awards are about its own player: `self` is its id.\n */\nexport function cleanAwards(awards, ids, self = null) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(awards)) return [];\n  const given = new Map();\n  const out = [];\n  for (const a of awards) {\n    const id = self ?? a?.id;\n    const title = String(a?.title ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.title);\n    if (!title || !ids.includes(id) || (given.get(id) || 0) >= HIGHLIGHTS.awards) continue;\n    given.set(id, (given.get(id) || 0) + 1);\n    const detail = String(a.detail ?? '').trim().slice(0, HIGHLIGHTS.detail);\n    out.push(detail ? { id, title, detail } : { id, title });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/**\n * Check a host's standings: groups of ids, best first, every present player\n * exactly once. Players already gone may be placed or left out; whoever is\n * left out lands in a last group of their own.\n */\nexport function checkStandings(standings, presentIds, allIds) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(standings)) return { ok: false, problem: 'standings is not an array' };\n  const all = new Set(allIds);\n  const seen = new Set();\n  const groups = [];\n  for (const group of standings) {\n    const ids = Array.isArray(group) ? group : [group];\n    const kept = [];\n    for (const id of ids) {\n      if (!Number.isInteger(id) || !all.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `unknown player id ${JSON.stringify(id)}` };\n      if (seen.has(id)) return { ok: false, problem: `player ${id} is placed twice` };\n      seen.add(id);\n      kept.push(id);\n    }\n    if (kept.length) groups.push(kept);\n  }\n  const missing = presentIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (missing.length) return { ok: false, problem: `standings leave out player${missing.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} ${missing.join(', ')}` };\n  const absent = allIds.filter((id) => !seen.has(id));\n  if (absent.length) groups.push(absent);\n  return { ok: true, standings: groups };\n}\n\n/**\n * @param {object} o\n * @param {number} o.round            round number, carried on every message\n * @param {{key:string, slot:number, name:string}[]} o.players\n * @param {string} o.hostKey          whose game runs a shared world\n * @param {string} [o.serverKey]      a copy with no player of its own that runs the shared world\n *                                    instead (a server): one more copy after the players, welcomed\n *                                    with server: true, never ranked; the round is void if it goes\n * @param {string|null} o.mode        parallel | ghost | shared-world, or an older tag (modeOf); null takes the first hello's\n * @param {number} o.seed\n * @param {number} o.limitMs\n * @param {{now:()=>number, setTimeout:Function, clearTimeout:Function}} [o.clock]\n * @param {(key:string, msg:object) => void} o.deliver\n * @param {(status:object) => void} [o.onStatus]\n * @param {(record:object) => void} [o.onEnd]\n * @param {boolean} [o.gate]          the hub shows a splash and collects the players' ready itself:\n *                                    games ready up once loaded, and the round starts on release()\n */\nexport function createRound({\n  round,\n  players,\n  hostKey,\n  mode = null,\n  seed,\n  limitMs,\n  clock = REAL_CLOCK,\n  deliver,\n  onStatus = () => {},\n  onEnd = () => {},\n  timings = TIMINGS,\n  gate = false,\n  serverKey = null,\n}) {\n  mode = modeOf(mode);\n  const t = { ...TIMINGS, ...timings };\n  const seats = [...players]\n    .sort((a, b) => a.slot - b.slot)\n    .map((p, id) => ({\n      id,\n      key: p.key,\n      slot: p.slot,\n      name: p.name,\n      color: SLOT_COLORS[p.slot % SLOT_COLORS.length],\n      hello: false,\n      ready: false,\n      out: null,\n      result: null,\n      /** The last progress score the hub saw: the result of a player who never reports one. */\n      progress: null,\n      stats: null,\n      awards: [],\n      caps: null,\n      hidden: null,\n    }));\n  const server = serverKey\n    ? { id: seats.length, key: serverKey, slot: null, name: 'Server', color: null, hello: false, ready: false, out: null, result: null, progress: null, stats: null, awards: [], caps: null, hidden: null }\n    : null;\n  /** Every copy in the round: the players, then the server when there is one. */\n  const copies = server ? [...seats, server] : seats;\n  const byKey = new Map(copies.map((s) => [s.key, s]));\n  const ids = seats.map((s) => s.id);\n  const host = server ?? byKey.get(hostKey) ?? seats[0];\n  const timers = new Set();\n  const issues = [];\n  let phase = 'loading';\n  let goAt = null;\n  let record = null;\n  let released = !gate;\n\n  const later = (ms, fn) => {\n    const handle = clock.setTimeout(() => {\n      timers.delete(handle);\n      fn();\n    }, Math.max(0, ms));\n    timers.add(handle);\n    return handle;\n  };\n  const cancel = (handle) => {\n    if (handle == null) return;\n    clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n    timers.delete(handle);\n  };\n\n  /** The players still in the round. */\n  const present = () => seats.filter((s) => !s.out);\n  /** The copies still in the round: the players, and the server. */\n  const presentCopies = () => copies.filter((s) => !s.out);\n  const selfReported = () => SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\n  const needsHost = () => !selfReported();\n  const send = (seat, msg) => deliver(seat.key, { round, ...msg });\n  const toPresent = (msg, except = null) => {\n    for (const s of presentCopies()) if (s !== except && s.hello) send(s, msg);\n  };\n  const issue = (seat, problem) => {\n    issues.push({ key: seat?.key ?? null, id: seat?.id ?? null, problem });\n    status();\n  };\n\n  function status() {\n    onStatus({\n      round,\n      phase,\n      mode,\n      host: host.id,\n      goAt,\n      gate,\n      released,\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({\n        id: s.id,\n        key: s.key,\n        slot: s.slot,\n        name: s.name,\n        color: s.color,\n        hello: s.hello,\n        ready: s.ready,\n        out: s.out,\n        result: s.result,\n        client: s.caps?.client ?? null,\n      })),\n      server: server && { id: server.id, key: server.key, hello: server.hello, ready: server.ready, out: server.out, client: server.caps?.client ?? null },\n      issues: issues.slice(),\n    });\n  }\n\n  function welcome(seat) {\n    send(seat, {\n      type: 'welcome',\n      me: seat.id,\n      host: host.id,\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, name: s.name, color: s.color })),\n      keys: copies.map((s) => s.key),\n      mode,\n      seed: seed >>> 0,\n      limitMs,\n      ...(gate ? { splash: true } : {}),\n      ...(seat === server ? { server: true } : {}),\n    });\n    for (const s of seats) if (s.out) send(seat, { type: 'leave', id: s.id, reason: s.out });\n  }\n\n  function markOut(seat, reason) {\n    if (seat.out || phase === 'ended') return;\n    seat.out = reason;\n    cancel(seat.hidden);\n    seat.hidden = null;\n    toPresent({ type: 'leave', id: seat.id, reason });\n    // A player who sat out is still at the hub: tell their game it is over for them.\n    if (reason === 'not-ready' && seat.hello) send(seat, { type: 'end', reason: 'sat-out' });\n  }\n\n  function settle() {\n    if (phase === 'ended') return;\n    const left = present();\n    if (!left.length) return finishVoid('no-players');\n    if (needsHost() && host.out) {\n      return finishVoid(host.out === 'not-ready' ? 'host-not-ready' : 'host-left', phase === 'loading' ? 'void' : 'host-left');\n    }\n    if (phase === 'loading') {\n      if (released && presentCopies().every((s) => s.ready)) begin();\n      return;\n    }\n    if (selfReported() && left.every((s) => s.result)) finishResults();\n  }\n\n  function begin() {\n    phase = 'countdown';\n    goAt = clock.now() + t.countdownMs;\n    toPresent({ type: 'start', at: goAt });\n    later(t.countdownMs, () => {\n      if (phase === 'countdown') {\n        phase = 'playing';\n        status();\n      }\n    });\n    later(t.countdownMs + limitMs, timeUp);\n    status();\n  }\n\n  function timeUp() {\n    if (phase === 'ended' || phase === 'grace') return;\n    phase = 'grace';\n    toPresent({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: t.graceMs });\n    later(t.graceMs, () => {\n      if (phase === 'ended') return;\n      if (selfReported()) finishResults();\n      else finishVoid('no-result');\n    });\n    status();\n  }\n\n  function finishResults() {\n    // A player still here who never reported is ranked by the last progress the hub saw from them.\n    const results = new Map(\n      seats.filter((s) => s.result || (!s.out && Number.isFinite(s.progress))).map((s) => [s.id, s.result ?? { score: s.progress, fallback: true }])\n    );\n    // Whoever reported and then left keeps their place: only those who left with nothing count as beaten.\n    const ranked = rankResults(results, seats.filter((s) => !s.out || s.result).map((s) => s.id));\n    const gone = seats.filter((s) => s.out && !s.result).map((s) => s.id);\n    const scores = {};\n    for (const [id, r] of results) scores[id] = Number.isFinite(r.time) ? r.time : r.score;\n    const stats = Object.fromEntries(seats.filter((s) => s.stats).map((s) => [s.id, s.stats]));\n    const awards = seats.flatMap((s) => s.awards);\n    finishPlayed(gone.length ? [...ranked, gone] : ranked, { scores, results: Object.fromEntries(results), stats, awards });\n  }\n\n  function finishPlayed(standings, extra = {}) {\n    end({ status: 'played', reason: 'finished', endReason: 'finished', standings, ...extra });\n  }\n\n  function finishVoid(reason, endReason = 'void') {\n    end({ status: 'void', reason, endReason, standings: null });\n  }\n\n  function end(outcome) {\n    if (phase === 'ended') return;\n    phase = 'ended';\n    for (const handle of timers) clock.clearTimeout(handle);\n    timers.clear();\n    const msg = { type: 'end', reason: outcome.endReason };\n    if (outcome.standings) msg.standings = outcome.standings;\n    toPresent(msg);\n    record = {\n      round,\n      mode,\n      hostId: host.id,\n      ...outcome,\n      players: seats.map((s) => ({ id: s.id, key: s.key, slot: s.slot, name: s.name, color: s.color, out: s.out })),\n      issues: issues.slice(),\n    };\n    status();\n    onEnd(record);\n  }\n\n  function receive(key, msg) {\n    const seat = byKey.get(key);\n    if (!seat || !msg || typeof msg.type !== 'string' || phase === 'ended' || seat.out) return;\n    switch (msg.type) {\n      case 'hello': {\n        if (seat.hello) return;\n        seat.hello = true;\n        seat.caps = { v: msg.v, client: msg.client, mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: msg.card === true };\n        if (msg.v !== 1) issue(seat, `hello speaks protocol ${JSON.stringify(msg.v)}, not 1`);\n        const said = modeOf(msg.mode);\n        if (!mode && said) mode = said;\n        else if (msg.mode && said !== mode) issue(seat, `hello says mode ${msg.mode}, the round is ${mode}`);\n        welcome(seat);\n        status();\n        return;\n      }\n      case 'ready':\n        if (!seat.hello || seat.ready || phase !== 'loading') return;\n        seat.ready = true;\n        status();\n        return settle();\n      case 'result': {\n        if (!selfReported()) return issue(seat, `result is for parallel and ghost; this round is ${mode}`);\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'result before start');\n        if (seat.result) return;\n        const time = asNumber(msg.time);\n        const score = asNumber(msg.score);\n        if (Number.isFinite(time)) seat.result = { time };\n        else if (Number.isFinite(score)) seat.result = { score };\n        else return issue(seat, 'result needs a finite time or score');\n        seat.stats = cleanStats(msg.stats);\n        seat.awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids, seat.id);\n        status();\n        return settle();\n      }\n      case 'finish': {\n        if (selfReported()) return issue(seat, `finish is for a shared world; ${mode} games report result`);\n        if (seat !== host) return issue(seat, 'finish from a player who is not the host');\n        if (phase === 'loading') return issue(seat, 'finish before start');\n        const checked = checkStandings(msg.standings, present().map((s) => s.id), ids);\n        if (!checked.ok) return issue(seat, `finish ignored: ${checked.problem}`);\n        const scores = msg.scores && typeof msg.scores === 'object' ? msg.scores : undefined;\n        const given = msg.stats && typeof msg.stats === 'object' ? msg.stats : {};\n        const stats = Object.fromEntries(ids.map((id) => [id, cleanStats(given[id])]).filter(([, v]) => v));\n        const awards = cleanAwards(msg.awards, ids);\n        // won makes it a team result; a game tagged co-op that leaves it out lost, as co-op always read it.\n        const won = typeof msg.won === 'boolean' ? msg.won : seat.caps?.mode === 'co-op' ? false : undefined;\n        return finishPlayed(checked.standings, { scores, won, stats, awards });\n      }\n      case 'error':\n        issue(seat, `game error: ${String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 200)}`);\n        if (msg.fatal) {\n          if (needsHost() && seat === host) return finishVoid('host-error');\n          markOut(seat, 'disconnected');\n          status();\n          settle();\n        }\n        return;\n      case 'vis':\n        if (seat !== host || !needsHost()) return;\n        if (msg.hidden && seat.hidden == null && phase !== 'loading') {\n          seat.hidden = later(t.hiddenMs, () => finishVoid('host-hidden'));\n        } else if (!msg.hidden) {\n          cancel(seat.hidden);\n          seat.hidden = null;\n        }\n        return;\n      default:\n        return issue(seat, `unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function leave(key, reason = 'left') {\n    const seat = byKey.get(key);\n    if (!seat || seat.out || phase === 'ended') return;\n    markOut(seat, reason);\n    status();\n    settle();\n  }\n\n  const sitOut = (test) => () => {\n    if (phase !== 'loading') return;\n    for (const s of copies) if (test(s) && !s.out) markOut(s, 'not-ready');\n    status();\n    settle();\n  };\n\n  function startRound() {\n    // A gated round waits on the hub's splash, however long it holds: only\n    // release() starts the clock on the games that are still loading.\n    if (!gate) {\n      later(t.helloMs, sitOut((s) => !s.hello));\n      later(t.readyMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\n    }\n    status();\n  }\n\n  /** The splash is over: start as soon as every game has loaded, and wait loadGraceMs at most for the slow ones. */\n  function release() {\n    if (released || phase !== 'loading') return;\n    released = true;\n    later(t.loadGraceMs, sitOut((s) => !s.ready));\n    status();\n    settle();\n  }\n\n  startRound();\n\n  return {\n    receive,\n    leave,\n    release,\n    /** Call time now, as the cap would: the host pressed \"End round\". */\n    timeUp() {\n      if (phase === 'countdown' || phase === 'playing') timeUp();\n    },\n    /** A player's progress score, as the hub's scoreboard saw it (parallel and ghost). */\n    progress(id, score) {\n      const seat = seats[id];\n      if (seat && !seat.out && !seat.result && Number.isFinite(score) && phase !== 'ended') seat.progress = score;\n    },\n    /** End the round now: the session ended, or the host skipped this game. */\n    abort(reason = 'skipped') {\n      finishVoid(reason, reason === 'session-ended' ? 'session-ended' : 'void');\n    },\n    get phase() {\n      return phase;\n    },\n    get released() {\n      return released;\n    },\n    get record() {\n      return record;\n    },\n    get mode() {\n      return mode;\n    },\n    seats: () => seats.map((s) => ({ ...s, hidden: undefined })),\n  };\n}\n","numLines":534,"startLine":1,"totalLines":534}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0164eF4y6uyuoDDbK2A5hDfh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
