rd and gamepad buttons together, sorted.\n2356:- `analog?: [number, number]`: The touch joystick and the gamepad's left stick (after its deadzone).\n2361:- `gamepad?: boolean`: Whether a gamepad is connected (`gamepadConnected`), when that changes.\n2374:- `readonly gamepad: boolean`\n2609:- `vibrato?: { depth: number; rate: number }`: Vibrato depth in semitones and rate in Hz.\n----\nGUIDE.md:41:  (paths are relative to the page). To ship one file with no `assets/` folder, set\nGUIDE.md:135:    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\nGUIDE.md:1006:| Console: \"Multiple instances of Three.js being imported\" | three.js loaded twice | use `THREE` from the bundle, nothing else |\nCHANGELOG.md:5:`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\nCHANGELOG.md:7:When a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nCHANGELOG.md:20:  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\nCHANGELOG.md:408:  bundled; it resolves to a `ModelCatalog` (`into` also adds the defs to one of yours).\nCHANGELOG.md:412:  Anyone else's work, CC0 included and a single file too, only from a pack (`source.pack`) whose\nCHANGELOG.md:821:- **The engine kit**: `npm run bundle` builds `pixel-engine.js`, one self-contained ES module\nAPI.md:45:Models every bundle carries: `ctx.loadModel('assets/hero.glb')` works with no files next to it.\nAPI.md:2743:- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is full, 0 for an unknown preset). Inline preset objects share one emitter per distinct content, so `burst({ ...literal }, at)` every…\nAPI.md:3030:base URL; a page may put a data URL for it in `__PIXEL_ASSETS__`, as single-file builds do for\