{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ef3rAxu3nrhRbSCQWmrAyt","type":"tool_result","content":"2762\t### class Hud\n2763\t\n2764\tPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\n2765\tthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\n2766\tlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n2767\t(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n2768\t\n2769\tRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n2770\t(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\n2771\tresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n2772\t\n2773\t  ctx.hud.clear();\n2774\t  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n2775\t  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n2776\t\n2777\t- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n2778\t- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n2779\t- `visible: boolean`\n2780\t- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n2781\t- `get height: number`\n2782\t- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n2783\t- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n2784\t- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n2785\t- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n2786\t- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n2787\t- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n2788\t- `dispose(): void`\n2789\t\n2790\t### type HudAnchor\n2791\t\n2792\t```ts\n2793\ttype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n2794\t```\n2795\t\n2796\tWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n2797\t\n2798\t### type HudColor\n2799\t\n2800\t```ts\n2801\ttype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n2802\t```\n2803\t\n2804\t### interface HudOptions\n2805\t\n2806\t- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n2807\t- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n2808\t- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n2809\t- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n2810\t\n2811\t### hudPlace()\n2812\t\n2813\t```ts\n2814\tfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n2815\t```\n2816\t\n2817\tTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n2818\t`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n2819\t\n2820\t## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n2821\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"d6624fc0-8802-4d5c-bfc3-51052ca4434e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:05.339Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"### class Hud\n\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type HudAnchor\n\n```ts\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n```\n\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n\n### type HudColor\n\n```ts\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n```\n\n### interface HudOptions\n\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n\n### hudPlace()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n```\n\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n\n## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":2762,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ef3rAxu3nrhRbSCQWmrAyt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
