{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BqFjQ934VcowVEJmb4Gqy9","type":"tool_result","content":"4606\t### interface Recording\n4607\t\n4608\t- `readonly format: 1`\n4609\t- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n4610\t- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.\n4611\t- `readonly args?: unknown`: What the game was made with (`Game.args`), when its name alone can't rebuild it.\n4612\t- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed (`ctx.random` comes from it and the game's name).\n4613\t- `readonly time: number`: Game time when the level began (`ctx.time` carries on across levels).\n4614\t- `readonly frames: readonly InputFrame[]`: Every frame the level ran, from its first.\n4615\t- `readonly truncated?: boolean`: True when the level ran longer than a recording keeps (the frames are its start).\n4616\t- `readonly from?: Snapshot`: The save-state the frames start from (`engine.restore()` began this recording), if any.\n4617\t- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…\n4618\t\n4619\t### recordingProblem()\n4620\t\n4621\t```ts\n4622\tfunction recordingProblem(v: unknown): string | null\n4623\t```\n4624\t\n4625\tIs `v` a recording this engine can replay? Returns the problem, or null.\n4626\t\n4627\t### class RenderView\n4628\t\n4629\t- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n4630\t- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n4631\t- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4632\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n4633\t- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n4634\t- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4635\t- `enabled: boolean`\n4636\t- `get texture: Texture`\n4637\t- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n4638\t- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n4639\t- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n4640\t- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n4641\t- `dispose(): void`\n4642\t\n4643\t### interface RenderViewOptions\n4644\t\n4645\t- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n4646\t- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n4647\t- `near?: number`\n4648\t- `far?: number`\n4649\t- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n4650\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"4b92379b-0b26-4ce5-bc9b-7623e98f9dd7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:07.331Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"### interface Recording\n\n- `readonly format: 1`\n- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.\n- `readonly args?: unknown`: What the game was made with (`Game.args`), when its name alone can't rebuild it.\n- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed (`ctx.random` comes from it and the game's name).\n- `readonly time: number`: Game time when the level began (`ctx.time` carries on across levels).\n- `readonly frames: readonly InputFrame[]`: Every frame the level ran, from its first.\n- `readonly truncated?: boolean`: True when the level ran longer than a recording keeps (the frames are its start).\n- `readonly from?: Snapshot`: The save-state the frames start from (`engine.restore()` began this recording), if any.\n- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…\n\n### recordingProblem()\n\n```ts\nfunction recordingProblem(v: unknown): string | null\n```\n\nIs `v` a recording this engine can replay? Returns the problem, or null.\n\n### class RenderView\n\n- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `enabled: boolean`\n- `get texture: Texture`\n- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface RenderViewOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n- `near?: number`\n- `far?: number`\n- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n","numLines":45,"startLine":4606,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BqFjQ934VcowVEJmb4Gqy9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
