{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHpp5W9qSfdAzmY3GkYMw7","type":"tool_result","content":"4881\t### class Timeline\n4882\t\n4883\t- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n4884\t- `readonly duration: number`\n4885\t- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n4886\t- `playing: boolean`\n4887\t- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n4888\t- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n4889\t- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n4890\t- `play(): void`\n4891\t- `pause(): void`\n4892\t- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n4893\t- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n4894\t- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n4895\t- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n4896\t- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n4897\t- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n4898\t\n4899\t### interface TimelineLine\n4900\t\n4901\t- `at: number`\n4902\t- `until: number`\n4903\t- `text: string`\n4904\t- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n4905\t\n4906\t### interface TimelineOptions\n4907\t\n4908\t- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n4909\t- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n4910\t- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n4911\t- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n4912\t- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n4913\t- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n4914\t\n4915\t### interface TraceRow\n4916\t\n4917\t- `name: string`\n4918\t- `kind: string`\n4919\t- `depth: number`\n4920\t- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n4921\t\n4922\t### class Trail\n4923\t\n4924\t- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n4925\t- `readonly capacity: number`\n4926\t- `width: number`\n4927\t- `life: number`\n4928\t- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n4929\t- `readonly tail: Color`\n4930\t- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n4931\t- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n4932\t- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n4933\t- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n4934\t- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n4935\t\n4936\t### interface TrailOptions\n4937\t\n4938\t- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939\t- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940\t- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941\t- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942\t- `tail?: number`\n4943\t- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n4944\t\n4945\t### TRANSITION_CELLS\n4946\t\n4947\t```ts\n4948\tconst TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4949\t```\n4950\t\n4951\tArt pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n4952\t\n4953\t### type TransitionKind\n4954\t\n4955\t```ts"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"8c3309db-bd30-4a26-a53f-dc83222b632b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:09.230Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n### interface TimelineOptions\n\n- `shots?: readonly CameraKey[]`\n- `cues?: readonly Cue[]`\n- `lines?: readonly Line[]`\n- `duration?: number`: Length (s); default the last key, cue or line.\n- `bars?: number`: Seconds the letterbox bars take to slide in and out (default 0.6; 0: no bars).\n- `onEnd?: () => void`: Called once when the playhead reaches the end (or the scene is skipped).\n\n### interface TraceRow\n\n- `name: string`\n- `kind: string`\n- `depth: number`\n- `status: Status | null`: This tick's answer, or null if this tick never reached the node.\n\n### class Trail\n\n- `new Trail(o: TrailOptions = {})`\n- `readonly capacity: number`\n- `width: number`\n- `life: number`\n- `readonly head: Color`: Head and tail colours (live: `trail.head.setHex(...)`).\n- `readonly tail: Color`\n- `push(p: Vector3, time: number): void`: The trail's newest point (call every frame while it moves).\n- `reset(): void`: Drop every point.\n- `get length: number`: Points alive now.\n- `update(time: number, camera: Camera): void`: Per frame: forget old points, rebuild the ribbon facing `camera`.\n- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n\n### interface TrailOptions\n\n- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n- `tail?: number`\n- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n\n### TRANSITION_CELLS\n\n```ts\nconst TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n```\n\nArt pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n\n### type TransitionKind\n\n```ts","numLines":75,"startLine":4881,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RHpp5W9qSfdAzmY3GkYMw7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkeFfumkSFF4XnAw6xbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0167NWppXodtnpbMnxXNHZEX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","offset":1249,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12624,"cache_read_input_tokens":155949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12624},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"272fad99-9e60-4a6b-a498-721f9d0455fb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:10.973Z","request_id":"req_011CgkeFfZByqEwDxEEthzcv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0167NWppXodtnpbMnxXNHZEX":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","offset":1249,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0167NWppXodtnpbMnxXNHZEX","type":"tool_result","content":"1249\t### class LightPool\n1250\t\n1251\tA fixed pool of point lights shared by many requests (see the file comment). Available\n1252\tto games as `ctx.lights` (sized by quality: low 4, medium 8, high 16), or create your\n1253\town with `new LightPool({ size, parent: scene })` and call `update` every frame.\n1254\t\n1255\t- `new LightPool(options: LightPoolOptions = {})`\n1256\t- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`\n1257\t- `readonly lights: PointLight[]`\n1258\t- `get size: number`: Number of real lights (constant unless `resize`d).\n1259\t- `request(options: LightRequestOptions = {}): LightHandle`: Ask for a light. Returns a handle to move, recolour or release.\n1260\t- `update(dt: number, focus: Vector3, range = 18): void`: Assign lights for this frame. `focus` is what the camera looks at; requests further than `range` + their radius from it are not lit. Call once per rendered frame.\n1261\t- `clear(): void`: Release every request at once and darken the lights (level unload).\n1262\t- `resize(size: number): void`: Change the number of real lights. Every material using lights recompiles once, so do it rarely (a quality change), never per frame.\n1263\t- `stats(): LightPoolStats`\n1264\t- `describe(): { id: number; name: string; score: number; slot: number; level: number; alive: boolean }[]`: Every live request with its score and slot (debugging, inspectors).\n1265\t- `dispose(): void`\n1266\t\n1267\t### interface LightPoolOptions\n1268\t\n1269\t- `size?: number`: Real lights in the pool (constant: changing it recompiles materials). Default 8.\n1270\t- `parent?: Object3D`: Parent for the pool's lights (added to it). Usually the scene.\n1271\t\n1272\t### interface LightPoolStats\n1273\t\n1274\t- `size: number`\n1275\t- `requests: number`\n1276\t- `lit: number`\n1277\t- `assignments: number`: Slot hand-overs since creation (a request got a light).\n1278\t- `waiting: number`: Requests that wanted a light but had to wait last frame.\n1279\t- `updateMs: number`: Milliseconds spent in the last update (CPU).\n1280\t\n1281\t### interface LightRequestOptions\n1282\t\n1283\t- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n1284\t- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n1285\t- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n1286\t- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n1287\t- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n1288\t- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n1289\t- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n1290\t- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n1291\t- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n1292\t- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n1293\t- `fadeOut?: number`\n1294\t- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n1295\t- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n1296\t\n1297\t### interface MergeOptions\n1298\t\n1299\t- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n1300\t- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n1301\t\n1302\t### mergeStaticMeshes()\n1303\t\n1304\t```ts\n1305\tfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n1306\t```\n1307\t\n1308\tMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"940dc13b-7e61-46c9-a994-1f31a31631bb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:24:10.984Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research/engine/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"### class LightPool\n\nA fixed pool of point lights shared by many requests (see the file comment). Available\nto games as `ctx.lights` (sized by quality: low 4, medium 8, high 16), or create your\nown with `new LightPool({ size, parent: scene })` and call `update` every frame.\n\n- `new LightPool(options: LightPoolOptions = {})`\n- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`\n- `readonly lights: PointLight[]`\n- `get size: number`: Number of real lights (constant unless `resize`d).\n- `request(options: LightRequestOptions = {}): LightHandle`: Ask for a light. Returns a handle to move, recolour or release.\n- `update(dt: number, focus: Vector3, range = 18): void`: Assign lights for this frame. `focus` is what the camera looks at; requests further than `range` + their radius from it are not lit. Call once per rendered frame.\n- `clear(): void`: Release every request at once and darken the lights (level unload).\n- `resize(size: number): void`: Change the number of real lights. Every material using lights recompiles once, so do it rarely (a quality change), never per frame.\n- `stats(): LightPoolStats`\n- `describe(): { id: number; name: string; score: number; slot: number; level: number; alive: boolean }[]`: Every live request with its score and slot (debugging, inspectors).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface LightPoolOptions\n\n- `size?: number`: Real lights in the pool (constant: changing it recompiles materials). Default 8.\n- `parent?: Object3D`: Parent for the pool's lights (added to it). Usually the scene.\n\n### interface LightPoolStats\n\n- `size: number`\n- `requests: number`\n- `lit: number`\n- `assignments: number`: Slot hand-overs since creation (a request got a light).\n- `waiting: number`: Requests that wanted a light but had to wait last frame.\n- `updateMs: number`: Milliseconds spent in the last update (CPU).\n\n### interface LightRequestOptions\n\n- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n- `fadeOut?: number`\n- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n\n### interface MergeOptions\n\n- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n\n### mergeStaticMeshes()\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n```\n\nMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M","numLines":60,"startLine":1249,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0167NWppXodtnpbMnxXNHZEX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
