{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011JF8ckKPTb3BoFqzVxgcCE","type":"tool_result","content":"# Credits (Pixel Engine 0.46.0)\n\nWhat this kit carries and where it came from, generated by `npm run bundle` from each built-in model's and texture's `source` (the data the engine repository's `npm run model -- credits` reads) and fr\n\n## Models and textures\n\n- **The engine's own work**, made in its repository: 151 of the 151 library models (`MODEL_LIBRARY`), 126 of the 126 textures (`TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/he\n- **kenney-castle** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/castle-kit/a395102d20-1711543616/kenney_castle-kit.\n- **kenney-furniture** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/furniture-kit/440e0608a4-1677580847/kenney_furni\n- **kenney-mini-dungeon** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/mini-dungeon/6cd72dc849-1785314274/kenney_min\n- **kenney-nature** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/nature-kit/37ac38a37b-1677698939/kenney_nature-kit.\n- **kenney-tiny-dungeon** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/tiny-dungeon/f8422efb44-1674742415/kenney_tin\n- **kenney-tiny-town** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/pages/assets/tiny-town/a415fbeb49-1735736916/kenney_tiny-town\n- **Your own imports** carry a `source` too (url, licence, author): credit them as their licence asks. A pack loaded with `loadPack` carries its models' and textures' `source`s.\n\n## Palettes\n\n- **Sweetie 16** by GrafxKid: the engine's 16 colours (`PALETTE`) and the `sweetie16` filter.\n- **PICO-8** by Lexaloffle Games (the PICO-8 fantasy console): the `pico8` filter.\n\n## Code\n\n- **three.js (three)** 0.186.0, MIT: https://threejs.org/. Its licence follows.\n- **Rapier (@dimforge/rapier3d)** 0.20.0, Apache-2.0: https://rapier.rs. Its licence follows.\n\n### three.js (three) licence\n\n```text\nThe MIT License\n\n21-15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `CameraKey`, `CameraShake`, `CameraShot`, `ClockState`, `cove\n22-\n23-## 1. Engine and games\n24-\n25-### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n26-\n27-```ts\n28-const ADAPTIVE_ASPECT: { readonly min: 0.4; readonly max: 2.4; }\n29-```\n30-\n31-Art aspect ratios (width / height) the adaptive mode allows; beyond them it letterboxes.\n32-\n33-### type AspectMode\n--\n3854:### HERO_CLIPS\n3855-\n3856-```ts\n3857:const HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\n3858-```\n3859-\n['Backflip', 'BellySlide', 'Climb', 'ClimbIdle', 'Crawl', 'Crouch', 'CrouchSlide', 'CrouchWalk', 'Fall', 'GetUp', 'GetUpFront', 'Grab', 'GroundPoundLand', 'GroundPoundSpin', 'Hang', 'HardLand', 'Idle', 'IdleLook', 'Land', 'LieDown', 'LieIdle', 'Prone', 'ProneDown', 'Pull', 'PullUp', 'Push', 'PushIdle', 'Run', 'ShimmyRight', 'SideFlip', 'Sit', 'SitDown', 'Skid', 'SkidTurn', 'Sleep', 'Slide', 'StandUp', 'StepDown', 'StepUp', 'Teeter', 'Tiptoe', 'TripleJump', 'Walk', 'WallSlide', 'Wave']\nno font string\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\n```\n\n### HERO_MODEL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_MODEL: \"assets/hero.glb\"\n```\n\n### HERO_RAGDOLL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RAGDOLL: readonly RagdollPart[]\n```\n\nThe hero as a ragdoll (the joints of `hero.glb`, see rig.ts): pelvis, torso and head, upper\narms and legs on ball joints held in cones, elbows and knees as hinges bending the way the\nclips bend them (Forearm −X, Shin +X). Hands and feet ride on their forearm and shin.\n\n### HERO_RIG\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RIG: RigSpec\n```\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n21:15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `\n22-\n23-## 1. Engine and games\n24-\n25-### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n26-\n27-```ts\n28-const ADAPTIVE_ASPECT: { readonly min: 0.4; readonly max: 2.4; }\n29-```\n30-\n31-Art aspect ratios (width / height) the adaptive mode allows; beyond them it letterboxes.\n--\n4733:### skyAt()\n4734-\n4735-```ts\n4736:function skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n4737-```\n4738-\n4739-The sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n4740-\n4741:### interface SkyState\n4742-\n4743-- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n4744-- `readonly sunColor: number`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"040198ea-2f0a-435f-8ccf-d3fd643b787a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:00:16.468Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Credits (Pixel Engine 0.46.0)\n\nWhat this kit carries and where it came from, generated by `npm run bundle` from each built-in model's and texture's `source` (the data the engine repository's `npm run model -- credits` reads) and fr\n\n## Models and textures\n\n- **The engine's own work**, made in its repository: 151 of the 151 library models (`MODEL_LIBRARY`), 126 of the 126 textures (`TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/he\n- **kenney-castle** by Kenney, Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (public domain dedication) (CC0-1.0, credit optional): https://kenney.nl/media/