{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WPQLEeVn5GpPMe1kUKozH","type":"tool_result","content":"- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\n1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\nexport * from './types/bundle';\n4836:### class Terrain\n4837-\n4838-- `new Terrain(o: TerrainOptions = {})`\n4839-- `readonly nx: number`\n4840-- `readonly nz: number`\n4841-- `readonly sizeX: number`\n4842-- `readonly sizeZ: number`\n4843-- `readonly at: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4844-- `readonly heights: Float32Array`: Heights at the grid points, row by row along z: `heights[ix + iz * (nx + 1)]`.\n4845-- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n4846-- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\n4847-- `get cell: [number, number]`: Metres between grid points along x and z.\n4848-- `pointX(ix: number): number`: World x, z of grid point (ix, iz).\n4849-- `pointZ(iz: number): number`\n4850-- `generate(f: (x: number, z: number) => number): this`: Fill the heights from `f(x, z)` (world x, z; metres above the terrain's origin), then redraw.\n4851-- `heightAt(x: number, z: number): number`: Height of the surface at world (x, z), in world y: the triangle it is over, as the mesh and the collider have it. Outside\n4852-- `normalAt(x: number, z: number, out = new Vector3()): Vector3`: The surface's normal at world (x, z) (central differences over half a cell).\n4853-- `update(): void`: Redraw the mesh from the heights (positions, flat normals, colours per face).\n4854-- `attach(physics: Physics): RAPIER.Collider`: Make (or remake, after `generate` / `erode`) the heightfield collider: a fixed body at the terrain's origin. Returns i\n4855-- `detach(): void`: Remove the collider (the mesh stays).\n4856-- `dispose(): void`: The collider and the mesh's geometry go (the shared material stays).\n4857-- `erode(o: ErosionOptions = {}): void`: Hydraulic erosion: `droplets` raindrops, each rolling downhill from a random point. A drop carries soil up to a capacity tha\n4858-\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4591-\n4592-### type PrecipitationKind\n4593-\n4594-```ts\n4595-type PrecipitationKind = 'rain' | 'snow'\n4596-```\n4598:### interface PrecipitationOptions\n4599-\n4600-- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4601-- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n4602-- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n4603-- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n4604-- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n4605-\n4606-### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n4609-- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n4610-- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"7aa561eb-78bc-4da6-86e8-83bd0eb687ae","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:04:49.317Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\n1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\nexport * from './types/bundle';\n4836:### class Terrain\n4837-\n4838-- `new Terrain(o: TerrainOptions = {})`\n4839-- `readonly nx: number`\n4840-- `readonly nz: number`\n4841-- `readonly sizeX: number`\n4842-- `readonly sizeZ: number`\n4843-- `readonly at: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4844-- `readonly heights: Float32Array`: Heights at the grid points, row by row along z: `heights[ix + iz * (nx + 1)]`.\n4845-- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n4846-- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\n4847-- `get cell: [number, number]`: Metres between grid points along x and z.\n4848-- `pointX(ix: number): number`: World x, z of grid point (ix, iz).\n4849-- `pointZ(iz: number): number`\n4850-- `generate(f: (x: number, z: number) => number): this`: Fill the heights from `f(x, z)` (world x, z; metres above the terrain's origin), then redraw.\n4851-- `heightAt(x: number, z: number): number`: Height of the surface at world (x, z), in world y: the triangle it is over, as the mesh and the collider have it. Outside\n4852-- `normalAt(x: number, z: number, out = new Vector3()): Vector3`: The surface's normal at world (x, z) (central differences over half a cell).\n4853-- `update(): void`: Redraw the mesh from the heights (positions, flat normals, colours per face).\n4854-- `attach(physics: Physics): RAPIER.Collider`: Make (or remake, after `generate` / `erode`) the heightfield collider: a fixed body at the terrain's origin. Returns i\n4855-- `detach(): void`: Remove the collider (the mesh stays).\n4856-- `dispose(): void`: The collider and the mesh's geometry go (the shared material stays).\n4857-- `erode(o: ErosionOptions = {}): void`: Hydraulic erosion: `droplets` raindrops, each rolling downhill from a random point. A drop carries soil up to a capacity tha\n4858-\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4591-\n4592-### type PrecipitationKind\n4593-\n4594-```ts\n4595-type PrecipitationKind = 'rain' | 'snow'\n4596-```\n4598:### interface PrecipitationOptions\n4599-\n4600-- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4601-- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n4602-- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n4603-- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n4604-- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n4605-\n4606-### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n4609-- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n4610-- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018WPQLEeVn5GpPMe1kUKozH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
