{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkhrm98GmjnTZJZpEcs7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011msUecrfXGTAtKw15VbnJG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='plan_part2.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"Selling returns 50% of the price. Prize cars can't be sold until a later patch of the fiction: \\\"Prize cars are not for sale. It is simply not done.\\\"\",\"Selling returns 50% of the price. Prize cars can't be sold: \\\"Prize cars are not for sale. It is simply not done.\\\"\")\nrep(\"Appendix B's car rows are the stock setups (a car's own `tyreMu` wins until the player changes tyres). `tyreTable` maps `dirt` and `gravel` to the factor; other surfaces use `SURFACES`.\",\"Appendix B's car rows are the stock setups: a car keeps its own `tyreMu`, `alphaP` and `tyreTable` until the player buys tyres. `tyreTable` maps `dirt` and `gravel` to the factor; other surfaces use `SURFACES`. Wear × goes in `wearX`.\")\nrep(\"**Licence A, \\\"National\\\".** Reward: 10,000 CR. All gold: Kite Cup Racer's tuned twin, or if already owned 25,000 CR.\",\"**Licence A, \\\"National\\\".** Reward: 10,000 CR. All gold: 25,000 CR and a gold helmet on the trophy shelf.\")\nrep(\"| **Tuning Street** | Seven tiles: Engine, Weight, Drivetrain, Suspension, Brakes, Aero, Tyres, Body (scroll by page). In a tile,\",\"| **Tuning Street** | Eight tiles, four to a page: Engine, Weight, Drivetrain, Suspension, Brakes, Aero, Tyres, Body. In a tile,\")\nrep(\"Also add `hub:type` (`Game`) and `hub:players` (`1-4`), as the hub's examples do.\",\"The hub's examples also carry `hub:type` and `hub:players`: use `Game`, and `1-2` for players on one device. Your exit interview's players field is `1–4`, counting sessions.\")\nrep(\"- Car body pitch, roll, heave; wheels steer and spin; rev-limiter shudder at idle; exhaust pop.\",\"- Car body pitch, roll, heave; wheels steer and spin; engine shake at idle and on the limiter; exhaust pop.\")\nrep(\"### Diorama\\n\",\"### Sky and night\\n\\n`applySky` gives a flat background, sun and ambient. Add depth: a far ring of silhouettes at 2 to 3 km per track (hills, mesas, skyline) in two or three flat palette colours, a sun or moon disc, a few chunky clouds. For night, raise `engine.ambient.intensity` until the road reads, then let baked lamp pools, `glow` windows and the headlight do the work. Raw `skyAt(21)` with no lights is close to black.\\n\\n### Diorama\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='plan_part1.md'; s=open(p).read()\nrep(\"### Assists (GT-like in spirit, plainly named in the UI)\",\"### Assists\")\nrep(\"| The engine's `Vehicle`? | A toy (default top speed 16 m/s, no gearbox, no load transfer). **Do not use it.** The tested car model in Appendix A replaces it |\",\"| The engine's `Vehicle`? | An arcade vehicle (default top speed 16 m/s, no gearbox, no load transfer), so tuning couldn't be felt. **Don't use it.** The tested car model in Appendix A replaces it |\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 tools/assemble.py ../PLAN.md && grep -n \"Gran Turismo\\|\\[GameTitle\\|exit-interview.json\\|GameTitle-SOURCE\\|claude-opus\" ../PLAN.md | head; grep -n \"{{\" ../PLAN.md | head -3; awk 'length > 0' ../PLAN.md | wc -l; wc -c ../PLAN.md; grep -c \"—\" ../PLAN.md","description":"Apply edits and assemble PLAN.md with embedded tested code","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2320,"cache_read_input_tokens":537833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2320},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":nu