{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Koz5whSoeGzDGYFwGZZPN3","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t## 4. Architecture\n101\t\n102\t### Stack\n103\t\n104\t- Pixel Engine as it ships. Unzip the kit into `src/` so `src/pixel-engine.js`, `src/check.mjs` and the docs sit together, and never edit `pixel-engine.js`. Your game lives in `src/game/`. Replace the starter: `src/index.html` loads `./main.js`, and `src/main.js` starts the game. Read the kit's `GUIDE.md` whole, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models.\n105\t- Plain modern JavaScript modules, esbuild to bundle (it's already installed). No other runtime libraries, no CDN.\n106\t- The hub client `session.js`, pasted unmodified as the first script after `<meta charset>`.\n107\t- Keep the hub's `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` in `tools/hub/`, for tests only. Fetch them with `gh api` or `curl` from the hub repository named in the brief.\n108\t\n109\t### Folder map\n110\t\n111\t```\n112\tsrc/                       the kit, unzipped (pixel-engine.js, check.mjs, docs...)\n113\tsrc/index.html, main.js    dev page and boot\n114\tsrc/game/app.js            App: profile, settings, input, audio mix, scene switching\n115\tsrc/game/sim/sim.js        Appendix A: tracks, car model, AI. Pure JS, no engine, no DOM\n116\tsrc/game/sim/race.js       RaceSim: field, laps, flags, starts, pit lane, slipstream, results, replay feed, events\n117\tsrc/game/sim/tuning.js     tunedParams(carId, install) → car parameters\n118\tsrc/game/sim/career.js     pure rules: money, licences, events, prizes, oil, days\n119\tsrc/game/data/             meta, cars, tyres, parts, tracks, licences, events, text, songs, about\n120\tsrc/game/input/            pad.js, actions.js, prompts.js\n121\tsrc/game/ui/               ui.js, widgets.js, glyphs.js, screens/*.js\n122\tsrc/game/scenes/           menu.js, race.js, replay.js\n123\tsrc/game/render/           trackmesh, dressing, carkit, carview, camera, sky, particles, skid\n124\tsrc/game/models/           cars.js, props.js, buildings.js (ModelDefs; `check.mjs --sheets` draws them)\n125\tsrc/game/audio/            mix, enginesynth, sfx, voice, music\n126\tsrc/game/net/              hub.js, couch.js\n127\tsrc/game/dev/devmode.js    src/game/attract/director.js\n128\ttools/build.mjs            makes the single HTML\n129\ttools/test.mjs             the one test command\n130\ttools/tests/               the suites\n131\ttools/medals.mjs           computes medal times from demonstrations\n132\tdocs/adding-content.md     how a designer adds a car, track, test or event\n133\t```\n134\t\n135\t### Scenes\n136\t\n137\tThree engine Games, each with `name`, `setup`, `fixedUpdate`, `update`, `cameraTarget`, `status`, `fingerprint`, `dispose`:\n138\t\n139\t- **MenuScene**: title, map, every menu set (showroom, parts street, service bay, garage, museum, licence centre, event hall, theatre foyer), each a Group that is shown or hidden. One music stream runs throughout.\n140\t- **RaceScene**: everything driven: race, licence test, test drive, time trial, attract clips, couch duel, hub round. Built from a `RaceSetup` plain object.\n141\t- **ReplayScene**: plays recorded poses with the replay director.\n142\t\n143\t`src/main.js` exports `createGame()` so `check.mjs --headless` and your tests can run it in Node. Guard all `document` access. In `update`, `status()` returns something like `race kestrel lap 2/3 p3/8 3:12.4` or `menu dealer focus=kite`. Set `window.__GAME__` in `ready(ctx)`, with `state()` (scene, screen, focus, race, profile), `press(action)`, and direct test hooks.\n144\t\n145\t### Simulation\n146\t\n147\t`RaceSim` is plain JS with no engine imports. `RaceScene.fixedUpdate` calls `sim.step(inputs)`, which runs 4 substeps of `stepCar` (240 Hz) for every car and `collideCars` per substep. Eight to twelve cars is nothing: the whole car table across all tracks runs in seconds in Node. It keeps previous poses so `update` can interpolate with `ctx.physics.alpha`. It emits an event queue (`shift`, `kerb`, `wallHit`, `carHit`, `lockup`, `lap`, `pitIn`, `flag`) that audio, particles and the HUD consume. `fingerprint(ctx)` returns a hash of quantised positions, laps and wear.\n148\t\n149\tThe engine's Rapier world stays empty apart from whatever a prop wants. Car-to-wall and car-to-car are in `sim.js`. Cones are a small circle check in `race.js`, then a tumble animation.\n150\t\n151\t### Input\n152\t\n153\t`src/game/input/pad.js`, once per frame at the end of `update`: read `navigator.getGamepads()` for each pad in standard mapping, quantise axes and triggers to 1/255, and if anything changed call `ctx.input.send({ pads: [...] })`. It arrives as `input.commands` next frame, so the engine's recordings replay it, at the cost of one frame of latency. Latch (engine fact 8).\n154\t\n155\t`src/game/input/actions.js` turns keys, mouse and latched pad state into per-player actions: `steer`, `throttle`, `brake`, `handbrake`, `shiftUp`, `shiftDown`, `camera`, `lookBack`, `pause`, `confirm`, `back`, `info`, `tabL`, `tabR`, `moveX`, `moveY`, with key repeat for menus (first repeat at 0.35 s, then every 0.09 s). It tracks the last device used for prompts, and it tracks idle time for attract mode (any key, pad change over 0.2, mouse move over 3 px, or touch resets it).\n156\t\n157\tFilters on driving input: keyboard steering goes toward ±1 at 3.2 per second and returns to 0 at 6 per second. Keyboard throttle and brake ramp over 0.1 s. Analog stick has an 8% radial deadzone and a gentle response curve (`|x|^1.4`), adjustable in Settings. A trigger that reports only 0 or 1 gets the keyboard ramp.\n158\t\n159\t### Saves\n160\t\n161\tProfile JSON in `localStorage` under a key from `TITLE`, with a version number and a migration switch. Wrap it in try/catch (`file://` and private modes can refuse). Save after every purchase, test and race. In a hub session the client supplies an empty storage; the game simply plays the round.\n162\t\n163\t### URL flags for development and tests\n164\t\n165\t`?scene=race&track=harbour&car=works&hour=21&rain=1&laps=2&ai=7&pace=0.92`, `?scene=licence&test=B-2`, `?scene=replay`, `?attract=1`, `?dev=1`, plus the engine's own (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`). Use `withUrlOptions` for the engine's.\n166\t\n167\t### Designer tools\n168\t\n169\tSo the rest of the game can be built later: all content is data in `src/game/data/`, validated by `tools/tests/data.mjs` (ids resolve, restrictions are satisfiable, every car has text, every test has medals). Track layouts are short corner lists. Models go through `check.mjs --sheets`. `docs/adding-content.md` shows, in a few lines each, how to add a car, track, test, event and song.\n170\t\n171\t---\n172\t\n173\t## 5. Driving and racing\n174\t\n175\tAppendix A is working code. Port it as is first, confirm the regression numbers in Appendix B, then extend it. Change numbers only with the regression test running.\n176\t\n177\t### The model, in words\n178\t\n179\tEach car has four wheels with loads from static weight, aero, heave, banking, and longitudinal and lateral transfer. Peak grip per tyre is `mu × load` with load sensitivity. Drive and brake forces share a friction circle with the slip-angle force. There is no wheel-spin state: the differential limits drive by what the wheels can carry, and overflow means wheelspin (rpm flare, smoke, lost side grip). That is why it is stable at 240 Hz and why layout matters: FF understeers under power, FR steps out if provoked, RR punishes a mid-corner lift, MR rotates quickly, 4WD digs out.\n180\t\n181\t### Assists\n182\t\n183\t| Assist | Default | Sim input | Effect |\n184\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n185\t| ABS | On | `abs` | Off: brakes can lock, tyres smoke and steering goes away; on: brakes stop at about 90% of what the tyre has left after cornering |\n186\t| Traction control 0–10 | 5 | `tcs` = value/10 | Trims drive to the driven tyres' remaining grip |\n187\t| Stability control 0–10 | 5 | `asm` = value/10 | Moment against yaw that grip doesn't explain |\n188\t| Automatic gears | On | `auto` | Off: L1/R1 or Q/E. Downshift refused if it would over-rev |\n189\t| Driving line | Off | render only | Dashes along the racing line, red where the speed profile says brake. The examiner offers it after three failed attempts at a test |\n190\t\n191\tLicence tests may force an assist off (the brief card says so). Assists live per profile and can be changed from the pause menu.\n192\t\n193\t### Starts, laps, finish\n194\t\n195\t- **Rolling start** for races: double file, 12 m apart, 150 m before the line, at 80 km/h. Everyone is held to 90 km/h (soft limiter) until the leader reaches the line; then green lights on the gantry. The player starts last of the field. Field sizes: 6 to 8.\n196\t- **Standing start** with five red lights for licence tests that ask for it, for the hub round, and for couch duels.\n197\t- **Race order** from laps and `s`. A lap counts when `s` wraps past 90% to under 10% going forward.\n198\t- **After the flag**, an AI takes the player's car for a cool-down lap, the camera drops to television cameras, and the results come up over it.\n199\t- **Slipstream.** Within 25 m behind another car and under 2 m laterally, above 100 km/h: `c.dragScale = 0.65`. Show a tiny icon and raise wind noise. It matters on Saltline.\n200\t- **Recovery.** Hold Triangle or R for 1 s when off the road or stopped: put the car on the racing line at this `s`, at zero speed, with 2 s of no-contact. AI cars do this by themselves after 3 s stopped. In a licence test, recovery ends the attempt.\n201\t- **Wrong way** sign when the heading opposes the tangent above 5 m/s.\n202\t- **Reverse.** Hold brake at a standstill for 0.4 s: reverse engages and the brake pedal drives it (`inp.reverse = true`, throttle from brake). Any throttle returns to first.\n203\t- **Rain.** `tr.muScale = 0.78`, an overcast sky, spray particles. One event round uses it; Dev mode and Arcade can set it anywhere.\n204\t\n205\t### AI\n206\t\n207\t`aiDrive` is pure pursuit with understeer feed-forward and a yaw damper, a speed target from `speedProfile`, and a lane shift to pass.\n208\t\n209\t- **Pace** is `skill`. Each event gives a range (section 6). Assign ascending by grid so the slowest starts at the front; that makes the player hunt through the field, and the leader is a rabbit.\n210\t- **Human touches:** a slow sine on `lane` (±0.6 m), and once a lap for low-pace cars a 2-second `skill − 0.04` lapse.\n211\t- **Rubber band:** off by default, a Dev slider up to ±3% of pace.\n212\t- **Field variety:** AI cars come from the event's pool, with `tunedParams` applied by event.\n213\t- **Endurance:** AI pits when mean wear is under 0.3 or fuel under 0.12.\n214\t- **Speed profiles** are per car and track: compute on the first race with that pair and cache them. `racingLine` runs once per track at load (a few ms).\n215\t\n216\t### Pit lane\n217\t\n218\tUsed on Kestrel, Harbour and Saltline (the three tracks with pit buildings, all on the start straight, on the driver's right). Data: `pit: { in: s, box: s, out: s }`. In that range set `tr.wallR` to `pitWidth + 2` so the barrier opens out, and set the surface to apron.\n219\t\n220\tCrossing the marked entry line at `t` inside the lane hands the car to an autopilot at 60 km/h to its box, where it stops. The crew runs: tyres (4 s if wear under 0.7), fuel (0.1 s per percent). Press Circle or Esc to skip tyres. Then the car drives out to the merge. A lap count continues through it. Show `PIT` and a stop timer. AI cars use the same autopilot.\n221\t\n222\t### Rally\n223\t\n224\tRed Clay's surface is `dirt`, with a `gravel` edge. Tyres matter through `tyreTable`. Each round is one-on-one against a rival, no contact (`rules.contact = false`), with a 3 s staggered start, time decides. The rival is rendered solid, and the HUD shows the gap. The crests launch cars at speed (0.66 s of air per 2 minutes in testing), so make landing a moment: dust, body bounce, a thump. On dirt, default stability control halves, and the handbrake (rear lock, 28% side grip) is how you rotate in hairpins.\n225\t\n226\t### Cameras\n227\t\n228\tChase near (6.8 m back, 2.4 up), chase far (8.5, 3.1), bonnet (0, 1.05, 0.2 on the car). Cycle with Triangle or C. Look-ahead 8 m, look height 1.1. FOV 58, rising to 66 with speed. Position spring ~8/s. Low-pass the camera's yaw a little so slides read: the camera shouldn't be nailed to the car. Hold Circle or B for look back. Right stick or right-drag orbits around the car and springs back. Small shake on kerbs and impacts via `engine.shake`. Recipe C3.\n229\t\n230\t### Replays\n231\t\n232\tRecord every car at 30 Hz into Float32Arrays: x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, steer, rpm, throttle, gear, flags (brake, sliding, airborne, in pit). Playback interpolates. Replays never re-simulate.\n233\t\n234\t**The director:** per track, auto-place camera posts every ~280 m at 15 to 25 m off the road and 3 to 8 m up (tele, FOV 18 to 30, tracking), and add a few authored shots per track (start-line low, helicopter on the straight, bridge or gantry). Pick the next post ahead of the focus car, cut every 4 to 8 s, and when a battle or a slide happens prefer that car. Bars and a small `REPLAY` tag top-left.\n235\t\n236\t**Controls:** Cross play/pause, left/right scrub, L1/R1 change focus car, Triangle change camera mode (Director, Chase, Bonnet, Free), R2 hold slow motion ×0.25. Mouse: click a car to focus it, drag to orbit in Free, wheel to zoom. HUD hide toggle for a clean view.\n237\t\n238\t**Saving:** keep the last race in memory. `Save` writes a compressed copy (10 Hz, Int16 quantised, base64) to storage, 3 slots, and refuses politely if storage is full. Time trial's best lap is stored the same way as the ghost.\n239\t\n240\t---\n241\t## 6. Content\n242\t\n243\tAll of this is data in `src/game/data/`. Physics rows for the cars and all track corners are in Appendix B.\n244\t\n245\t### World\n246\t\n247\tThe **Halcyon Peninsula**: a fictional stretch of coast, mountains and salt flats with a long, slightly eccentric love of motor cars. People here wash their cars on Sundays and argue about tyre pressures at weddings.\n248\t\n249\t### Marques and cars\n250\t\n251\t| Id | Car | Year | Layout | PS | kg | Price (CR) | Where |\n252\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n253\t| pico | Tsubame Pico 660 | 1991 | FF | 64 | 720 | 4,800 | Used lot |\n254\t| kite | Tsubame Kite 1.6 RS | 1996 | FF | 148 | 1,040 | 12,500 | Used lot |\n255\t| ginga | Kaminari Ginga S | 1994 | FR | 205 | 1,230 | 14,800 | Used lot |\n256\t| moth | Castellan Moth 1.8 | 1998 | FR | 135 | 860 | 24,000 | Dealer |\n257\t| ryu | Kaminari Ryu 2.0T | 1999 | 4WD turbo | 280 | 1,340 | 39,000 | Dealer |\n258\t| longhorn | Ironwood Longhorn 428 | 1969 | FR | 420 | 1,610 | 47,000 | Dealer |\n259\t| brandt32 | Brandt 3.2 CSR | 2000 | FR | 320 | 1,450 | 58,000 | Dealer |\n260\t| heck | Brandt Heck 3.6 | 1997 | RR | 360 | 1,380 | 92,000 | Dealer |\n261\t| libeccio | Vespucci Libeccio | 1995 | MR | 380 | 1,250 | 135,000 | Dealer |\n262\t| kiteCup | Tsubame Kite Cup Racer | 2000 | FF | 210 | 930 | Prize | Featherweight Trophy |\n263\t| ryuRally | Kaminari Ryu Rally Spec | 1999 | 4WD turbo | 330 | 1,230 | Prize | Red Clay Rally |\n264\t| works | Kaminari Ginga Works GT | 2000 | FR | 560 | 1,180 | Prize, then 310,000 | Harbour Lights 200 |\n265\t| corsa | Vespucci Libeccio Corsa | 1998 | MR | 620 | 1,100 | Prize, then 520,000 | Peninsula Touring Trophy |\n266\t| type9 | Halcyon Type 9 Prototype | 2001 | MR | 780 | 930 | Prize only | The Halcyon Grand Prix |\n267\t\n268\tMarque personalities, for text and badges: **Tsubame** (small, clever, swallow badge), **Kaminari** (thunder; serious Japanese-flavoured performance), **Castellan** (English; a shed, a lathe, a principle), **Brandt** (German-flavoured engineering, polite and terrifying), **Ironwood** (American; displacement as a moral position), **Vespucci** (Italian-flavoured; beautiful, a little dramatic), **Halcyon Works** (the Peninsula's own tiny race shop).\n269\t\n270\tStarting credits: **15,000**. All three used cars are affordable, and buying the Kite or Ginga leaves very little: that is the point.\n271\t\n272\tSelling returns 50% of the price. You can't sell your last car, so no save can get stuck. Prize cars can't be sold: \"Prize cars are not for sale. It is simply not done.\"\n273\t\n274\t### Tyres\n275\t\n276\t| Tyre | `tyreMu` | `alphaP` | dirt, gravel factor | Wear × | Price |\n277\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n278\t| Street | 0.95 | 0.14 | 0.45 | 0.8 | Fitted to Pico |\n279\t| Sport | 1.00 | 0.125 | 0.50 | 1.0 | 1,200 |\n280\t| Semi-slick | 1.12 | 0.115 | 0.42 | 1.4 | 4,800 |\n281\t| Racing slick | 1.30 | 0.105 | 0.35 | 2.2 | 12,000 |\n282\t| Rally dirt | 0.84 | 0.17 | 0.72 | 1.2 | 2,500 |\n283\t\n284\tAppendix B's car rows are the stock setups: a car keeps its own `tyreMu`, `alphaP` and `tyreTable` until the player buys tyres. `tyreTable` maps `dirt` and `gravel` to the factor; other surfaces use `SURFACES`. Wear × goes in `wearX`.\n285\t\n286\t### Parts\n287\t\n288\tEach one changes numbers in `tunedParams`. \"Slider\" means a setting becomes available on the Setup tab once bought. Each visible result is listed.\n289\t\n290\t| Category | Part | Effect | Price |\n291\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n292\t| Engine | Sport exhaust | power ×1.04; louder, deeper engine sound and crackle on lift | 900 |\n293\t| Engine | Intake and ECU | power ×1.06 | 1,800 |\n294\t| Engine | Stage 1, 2, 3 (exclusive) | power ×1.10, ×1.20, ×1.35; `rpmPeak` +0, +200, +400; `redline` and `upshift` +0, +200, +500 | 3,000, 8,000, 20,000 |\n295\t| Engine | Turbo kit 1, 2 (exclusive) | Turbo cars: power ×1.15, ×1.35. Others: ×1.25, ×1.50 and `turbo: true`, `turboLag: 0.8`; turbo whistle and blow-off appear | 6,000, 15,000 |\n296\t| Weight | Stage 1, 2, 3 (exclusive) | mass ×0.95, ×0.90, ×0.85; `cgH` ×0.99, ×0.98, ×0.96 | 1,500, 4,500, 12,000 |\n297\t| Drivetrain | Clutch and flywheel | `shiftTime` 0.11 | 1,200 |\n298\t| Drivetrain | Race gearbox | `shiftTime` 0.08; slider: Gearing (`final` ×0.85 to ×1.15, labelled ACCELERATION to TOP SPEED) | 5,000 |\n299\t| Drivetrain | Limited-slip diff | slider: LSD (`lsd` 0.2 to 0.8) | 2,500 |\n300\t| Suspension | Sport | `loadK` 0.085, `cgH` ×0.96; slider: Balance (`rollF` 0.45 to 0.70, labelled TURNS IN to STABLE) | 2,000 |\n301\t| Suspension | Race | `loadK` 0.07, `cgH` ×0.92; sliders: Balance, Ride height (`cgH` a further ×1.00 to ×0.90; below ×0.94 kerbs jolt the body) | 6,000 |\n302\t| Brakes | Sport pads | `brakeG` +0.15 | 1,500 |\n303\t| Brakes | Race kit | `brakeG` +0.40; slider: Balance (`brakeF` 0.50 to 0.75) | 5,000 |\n304\t| Aero | Street kit | `clA` +0.15, `cdA` +0.02; a lip spoiler appears on the model | 2,500 |\n305\t| Aero | Big wing | `clA` +0.50, `cdA` +0.06; slider: Downforce (×0.5 to ×1.5); a large wing appears on the model | 6,000 |\n306\t| Tyres | see table | | |\n307\t| Body | Paint (any of the 16 palette colours) | Model recolours, shown under showroom lights | 500 |\n308\t| Body | Rims (4 styles) | Hub colour and spoke pattern change | 300 |\n309\t\n310\tDisplayed power and weight come from `tunedParams`. Event limits read those numbers. Engine sound follows `rpmPeak` and exhaust. Show a dyno pull (section 9) on buying any engine part: the before and after curve drawn in the HUD, with the engine sound rising.\n311\t\n312\t### Service Bay\n313\t\n314\t- **Oil change, 250 CR.** Each 40 km after the first 200 km since a change takes 0.5% of power, down to −8%. `c.oil` carries it. A fresh change gives a small bonus of +2% for the first 100 km. The mechanic says so in one line.\n315\t- **Car wash, 50 CR.** No performance effect (\"It is simply polite.\"). Mud builds up on dirt (`dirt` 0..1 on the car) and the wash removes it: see section 8.\n316\t\n317\t### Licences\n318\t\n319\tEach test is data: `{ id, title, carId, track, startS, startSpeed, standing, end, limits, assists, medals, brief, tip, demo }`. `limits` says what fails the attempt (off the road, a stop outside the box, recovery). Times run from the first movement, or from the start line for rolling tests. Compute `medals` with `tools/medals.mjs`: run the AI demonstration in the sim at `skill: 0.97`, time T, then gold = T×1.03, silver = T×1.09, bronze = T×1.18, rounded to 0.01 s, and freeze the numbers in the data. A test passes at bronze. A licence is won when all four tests have at least bronze.\n320\t\n321\t`Cn` below is corner index n of that track's list (`tr.cornerS[n]` is its apex).\n322\t\n323\t**Licence C, \"Provisional\".** Car: Kite (stock, street tyres). Track: Proving Ground. Reward: 2,000 CR. All gold: the Pico as a prize.\n324\t\n325\t| Id | Title | Section | Lesson |\n326\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n327\t| C-1 | Start and Stop | Standing, 400 m along the long straight, stop inside a 30 m white box | The brake is a pedal with a far end |\n328\t| C-2 | First Corner | Rolling 60 km/h, C0 −100 m to C1 +100 m | Turn in, apex, unwind |\n329\t| C-3 | Cone Weave | Rolling 50 km/h down the straight through 6 cones at 40 m spacing. A hit cone adds 1 s | Weight moves |\n330\t| C-4 | The Short Loop | C2 −50 m to C6 +50 m | Link corners, keep your head up |\n331\t\n332\t**Licence B, \"Club\".** Car: Ginga. Reward: 5,000 CR. All gold: Castellan Moth as a prize.\n333\t\n334\t| Id | Title | Section | Lesson |\n335\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n336\t| B-1 | Threshold | Proving straight, rolling 160 km/h, ABS off, stop inside a box 150 m on. Locking up is allowed and costs time | Squeeze, don't stamp |\n337\t| B-2 | Hairpin Exit | Kestrel, C5 −150 m to C7 +60 m. Traction control 0 | Feed the throttle |\n338\t| B-3 | Three Layouts | Proving C7 to C10, driven three times in Kite, Ginga, Ryu; times added | FF, FR, 4WD in the same corners |\n339\t| B-4 | One Lap of Kestrel | Kestrel, flying lap | Rhythm |\n340\t\n341\t**Licence A, \"National\".** Reward: 10,000 CR. All gold: 25,000 CR and a gold helmet on the trophy shelf.\n342\t\n343\t| Id | Title | Car | Section | Lesson |\n344\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n345\t| A-1 | Blind Crest | Brandt 3.2 | Cedar, C3 −100 m to C5 +100 m | Trust the road you remember |\n346\t| A-2 | Switchbacks | Moth | Cedar, C7 to C10, uphill | Momentum |\n347\t| A-3 | Red Clay | Ryu Rally | Red Clay, C7 to C10, dirt | Rotate with the handbrake |\n348\t| A-4 | Harbour at Night | Libeccio | Harbour Lights, flying lap, no margin for error | Everything, by lamplight |\n349\t\n350\tAfter each attempt: medal, time, gap to the next medal, then **Retry**, **Watch your replay**, **Demonstration** (the AI drives it, label `DEMONSTRATION`, examiner's voice over), **Back**. Three failures in a row: the examiner offers the Driving line for this test.\n351\t\n352\t### Events\n353\t\n354\tPoints per round: 10, 8, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. Most points wins the series. Prize money is paid every round to the top four in the ratio 100%, 60%, 40%, 20%. The Bonus and prize car come only from winning the series. Each race advances the day counter.\n355\t\n356\t| Id | Event | Needs | Restriction | Rounds (track, laps) | AI pace | AI pool | 1st prize | Bonus |\n357\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n358\t| dawn | Dawn Patrol Cup | C | ≤210 PS | Kestrel 2; Harbour at dusk 2; Kestrel 3 | .86–.90 | Pico, Kite, Moth | 1,500 | 3,000 |\n359\t| fellow | Front-Drive Fellowship | C | FF, ≤230 PS | Cedar 2; Saltline 4 | .88–.91 | Kite, Kite (tuned), Pico (tuned) | 2,000 | 5,000 |\n360\t| feather | Featherweight Trophy | B | ≤1,100 kg | Cedar 3; Kestrel 3; Harbour at dusk 3 | .90–.93 | Moth, Kite Cup, Pico (tuned) | 3,000 | 8,000 + Kite Cup Racer |\n361\t| society | Rear-Drive Society | B | FR | Kestrel in rain 3; Saltline 5 | .91–.94 | Ginga, Brandt 3.2, Longhorn | 3,500 | 10,000 |\n362\t| clay | Red Clay Rally | B | Any; dirt tyres advised | Red Clay, 2 laps, 3 legs against one rival each | .91–.95 | Ryu, Ryu Rally | 4,000 | Ryu Rally Spec |\n363\t| touring | Peninsula Touring Trophy | A | ≤520 PS | Cedar 3; Harbour at night 3; Saltline 6; Kestrel 4 | .93–.96 | Brandt 3.2, Heck, Libeccio, Longhorn, Ryu (tuned) | 6,000 | 40,000 + Libeccio Corsa |\n364\t| h200 | Harbour Lights 200 | A | Any | Harbour, 10 laps, dusk into night, one stop needed, field of 8 | .92–.95 | Heck, Libeccio, Brandt 3.2 (tuned) | 20,000 | Ginga Works GT |\n365\t| gp | The Halcyon Grand Prix | A and Touring or H200 won | Any | Kestrel 5; Cedar 5; Saltline 8; Harbour at night 5 | .96–.99 | Works, Corsa, Libeccio (tuned) | 30,000 | Type 9, ending |\n366\t\n367\tTwenty-two races and twelve tests is about three hours for a new player. The ten-lap endurance needs exactly one stop at default rates: in testing, tyres fall to zero by lap 9 and the tank empties on lap 9 or 10, and lap time drifts from 117 s to 135 s. Short races use `wearRate` ×0.5.\n368\t\n369\t**Winning the GP:** a podium scene, the Type 9 reveal, then the credits, then the ending card, in the catalogue voice: \"You may keep driving. Most people do.\"\n370\t\n371\t### Arcade\n372\t\n373\tThe Arcade Gate on the map skips the career: **Quick Race** (any track, any car, laps, field size, Easy .85 / Normal .92 / Hard .98, hour, rain), **Time Trial** (any track and car, ghost of your best), **Couch Duel** (section 14). Every car and track is open here from the first minute, so someone trying the demo can see everything quickly. It pays no credits.\n374\t\n375\t### Home Garage and Museum\n376\t\n377\t**Home Garage:** your cars on a turntable with mileage, oil, wear and setup; choose your ride; sell; a trophy shelf with a 3D cup or medal for every win; your stats (days, km, wins, gold medals, % collected).\n378\t\n379\t**Museum:** all 14 cars with their brochure text and silhouette (unowned cars show as a dark silhouette until seen in a race), plus a page per track: map, length, corners, records.\n380\t\n381\t---\n382\t\n383\t## 7. Screens and controls\n384\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66624378-a7bb-42a2-8c1d-fc63666b5654","uuid":"1f2600d3-bc1a-498e-9b9a-f82cc2db8b85","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:16:54.679Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 4. Architecture\n\n### Stack\n\n- Pixel Engine as it ships. Unzip the kit into `src/` so `src/pixel-engine.js`, `src/check.mjs` and the docs sit together, and never edit `pixel-engine.js`. Your game lives in `src/game/`. Replace the starter: `src/index.html` loads `./main.js`, and `src/main.js` starts the game. Read the kit's `GUIDE.md` whole, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models.\n- Plain modern JavaScript modules, esbuild to bundle (it's already installed). No other runtime libraries, no CDN.\n- The hub client `session.js`, pasted unmodified as the first script after `<meta charset>`.\n- Keep the hub's `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` in `tools/hub/`, for tests only. Fetch them with `gh api` or `curl` from the hub repository named in the brief.\n\n### Folder map\n\n```\nsrc/                       the kit, unzipped (pixel-engine.js, check.mjs, docs...)\nsrc/index.html, main.js    dev page and boot\nsrc/game/app.js            App: profile, settings, input, audio mix, scene switching\nsrc/game/sim/sim.js        Appendix A: tracks, car model, AI. Pure JS, no engine, no DOM\nsrc/game/sim/race.js       RaceSim: field, laps, flags, starts, pit lane, slipstream, results, replay feed, events\nsrc/game/sim/tuning.js     tunedParams(carId, install) → car parameters\nsrc/game/sim/career.js     pure rules: money, licences, events, prizes, oil, days\nsrc/game/data/             meta, cars, tyres, parts, tracks, licences, events, text, songs, about\nsrc/game/input/            pad.js, actions.js, prompts.js\nsrc/game/ui/               ui.js, widgets.js, glyphs.js, screens/*.js\nsrc/game/scenes/           menu.js, race.js, replay.js\nsrc/game/render/           trackmesh, dressing, carkit, carview, camera, sky, particles, skid\nsrc/game/models/           cars.js, props.js, buildings.js (ModelDefs; `check.mjs --sheets` draws them)\nsrc/game/audio/            mix, enginesynth, sfx, voice, music\nsrc/game/net/              hub.js, couch.js\nsrc/game/dev/devmode.js    src/game/attract/director.js\ntools/build.mjs            makes the single HTML\ntools/test.mjs             the one test command\ntools/tests/               the suites\ntools/medals.mjs           computes medal times from demonstrations\ndocs/adding-content.md     how a designer adds a car, track, test or event\n```\n\n### Scenes\n\nThree engine Games, each with `name`, `setup`, `fixedUpdate`, `update`, `cameraTarget`, `status`, `fingerprint`, `dispose`:\n\n- **MenuScene**: title, map, every menu set (showroom, parts street, service bay, garage, museum, licence centre, event hall, theatre foyer), each a Group that is shown or hidden. One music stream runs throughout.\n- **RaceScene**: everything driven: race, licence test, test drive, time trial, attract clips, couch duel, hub round. Built from a `RaceSetup` plain object.\n- **ReplayScene**: plays recorded poses with the replay director.\n\n`src/main.js` exports `createGame()` so `check.mjs --headless` and your tests can run it in Node. Guard all `document` access. In `update`, `status()` returns something like `race kestrel lap 2/3 p3/8 3:12.4` or `menu dealer focus=kite`. Set `window.__GAME__` in `ready(ctx)`, with `state()` (scene, screen, focus, race, profile), `press(action)`, and direct test hooks.\n\n### Simulation\n\n`RaceSim` is plain JS with no engine imports. `RaceScene.fixedUpdate` calls `sim.step(inputs)`, which runs 4 substeps of `stepCar` (240 Hz) for every car and `collideCars` per substep. Eight to twelve cars is nothing: the whole car table across all tracks runs in seconds in Node. It keeps previous poses so `update` can interpolate with `ctx.physics.alpha`. It emits an event queue (`shift`, `kerb`, `wallHit`, `carHit`, `lockup`, `lap`, `pitIn`, `flag`) that audio, particles and the HUD consume. `fingerprint(ctx)` returns a hash of quantised positions, laps and wear.\n\nThe engine's Rapier world stays empty apart from whatever a prop wants. Car-to-wall and car-to-car are in `sim.js`. Cones are a small circle check in `race.js`, then a tumble animation.\n\n### Input\n\n`src/game/input/pad.js`, once per frame at the end of `update`: read `navigator.getGamepads()` for each pad in standard mapping, quantise axes and triggers to 1/255, and if anything changed call `ctx.input.send({ pads: [...] })`. It arrives as `input.commands` next frame, so the engine's recordings replay it, at the cost of one frame of latency. Latch (engine fact 8).\n\n`src/game/input/actions.js` turns keys, mouse and latched pad state into per-player actions: `steer`, `throttle`, `brake`, `handbrake`, `shiftUp`, `shiftDown`, `camera`, `lookBack`, `pause`, `confirm`, `back`, `info`, `tabL`, `tabR`, `moveX`, `moveY`, with key repeat for menus (first repeat at 0.35 s, then every 0.09 s). It tracks the last device used for prompts, and it tracks idle time for attract mode (any key, pad change over 0.2, mouse move over 3 px, or touch resets it).\n\nFilters on driving input: keyboard steering goes toward ±1 at 3.2 per second and returns to 0 at 6 per second. Keyboard throttle and brake ramp over 0.1 s. Analog stick has an 8% radial deadzone and a gentle response curve (`|x|^1.4`), adjustable in Settings. A trigger that reports only 0 or 1 gets the keyboard ramp.\n\n### Saves\n\nProfile JSON in `localStorage` under a key from `TITLE`, with a version number and a migration switch. Wrap it in try/catch (`file://` and private modes can refuse). Save after every purchase, test and race. In a hub session the client supplies an empty storage; the game simply plays the round.\n\n### URL flags for development and tests\n\n`?scene=race&track=harbour&car=works&hour=21&rain=1&laps=2&ai=7&pace=0.92`, `?scene=licence&test=B-2`, `?scene=replay`, `?attract=1`, `?dev=1`, plus the engine's own (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`). Use `withUrlOptions` for the engine's.\n\n### Designer tools\n\nSo the rest of the game can be built later: all content is data in `src/game/data/`, validated by `tools/tests/data.mjs` (ids resolve, restrictions are satisfiable, every car has text, every test has medals). Track layouts are short corner lists. Models go through `check.mjs --sheets`. `docs/adding-content.md` shows, in a few lines each, how to add a car, track, test, event and song.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Driving and racing\n\nAppendix A is working code. Port it as is first, confirm the regression numbers in Appendix B, then extend it. Change numbers only with the regression test running.\n\n### The model, in words\n\nEach car has four wheels with loads from static weight, aero, heave, banking, and longitudinal and lateral transfer. Peak grip per tyre is `mu × load` with load sensitivity. Drive and brake forces share a friction circle with the slip-angle force. There is no wheel-spin state: the differential limits drive by what the wheels can carry, and overflow means wheelspin (rpm flare, smoke, lost side grip). That is why it is stable at 240 Hz and why layout matters: FF understeers under power, FR steps out if provoked, RR punishes a mid-corner lift, MR rotates quickly, 4WD digs out.\n\n### Assists\n\n| Assist | Default | Sim input | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ABS | On | `abs` | Off: brakes can lock, tyres smoke and steering goes away; on: brakes stop at about 90% of what the tyre has left after cornering |\n| Traction control 0–10 | 5 | `tcs` = value/10 | Trims drive to the driven tyres' remaining grip |\n| Stability control 0–10 | 5 | `asm` = value/10 | Moment against yaw that grip doesn't explain |\n| Automatic gears | On | `auto` | Off: L1/R1 or Q/E. Downshift refused if it would over-rev |\n| Driving line | Off | render only | Dashes along the racing line, red where the speed profile says brake. The examiner offers it after three failed attempts at a test |\n\nLicence tests may force an assist off (the brief card says so). Assists live per profile and can be changed from the pause menu.\n\n### Starts, laps, finish\n\n- **Rolling start** for races: double file, 12 m apart, 150 m before the line, at 80 km/h. Everyone is held to 90 km/h (soft limiter) until the leader reaches the line; then green lights on the gantry. The player starts last of the field. Field sizes: 6 to 8.\n- **Standing start** with five red lights for licence tests that ask for it, for the hub round, and for couch duels.\n- **Race order** from laps and `s`. A lap counts when `s` wraps past 90% to under 10% going forward.\n- **After the flag**, an AI takes the player's car for a cool-down lap, the camera drops to television cameras, and the results come up over it.\n- **Slipstream.** Within 25 m behind another car and under 2 m laterally, above 100 km/h: `c.dragScale = 0.65`. Show a tiny icon and raise wind noise. It matters on Saltline.\n- **Recovery.** Hold Triangle or R for 1 s when off the road or stopped: put the car on the racing line at this `s`, at zero speed, with 2 s of no-contact. AI cars do this by themselves after 3 s stopped. In a licence test, recovery ends the attempt.\n- **Wrong way** sign when the heading opposes the tangent above 5 m/s.\n- **Reverse.** Hold brake at a standstill for 0.4 s: reverse engages and the brake pedal drives it (`inp.reverse = true`, throttle from brake). Any throttle returns to first.\n- **Rain.** `tr.muScale = 0.78`, an overcast sky, spray particles. One event round uses it; Dev mode and Arcade can set it anywhere.\n\n### AI\n\n`aiDrive` is pure pursuit with understeer feed-forward and a yaw damper, a speed target from `speedProfile`, and a lane shift to pass.\n\n- **Pace** is `skill`. Each event gives a range (section 6). Assign ascending by grid so the slowest starts at the front; that makes the player hunt through the field, and the leader is a rabbit.\n- **Human touches:** a slow sine on `lane` (±0.6 m), and once a lap for low-pace cars a 2-second `skill − 0.04` lapse.\n- **Rubber band:** off by default, a Dev slider up to ±3% of pace.\n- **Field variety:** AI cars come from the event's pool, with `tunedParams` applied by event.\n- **Endurance:** AI pits when mean wear is under 0.3 or fuel under 0.12.\n- **Speed profiles** are per car and track: compute on the first race with that pair and cache them. `racingLine` runs once per track at load (a few ms).\n\n### Pit lane\n\nUsed on Kestrel, Harbour and Saltline (the three tracks with pit buildings, all on the start straight, on the driver's right). Data: `pit: { in: s, box: s, out: s }`. In that range set `tr.wallR` to `pitWidth + 2` so the barrier opens out, and set the surface to apron.\n\nCrossing the marked entry line at `t` inside the lane hands the car to an autopilot at 60 km/h to its box, where it stops. The crew runs: tyres (4 s if wear under 0.7), fuel (0.1 s per percent). Press Circle or Esc to skip tyres. Then the car drives out to the merge. A lap count continues through it. Show `PIT` and a stop timer. AI cars use the same autopilot.\n\n### Rally\n\nRed Clay's surface is `dirt`, with a `gravel` edge. Tyres matter through `tyreTable`. Each round is one-on-one against a rival, no contact (`rules.contact = false`), with a 3 s staggered start, time decides. The rival is rendered solid, and the HUD shows the gap. The crests launch cars at speed (0.66 s of air per 2 minutes in testing), so make landing a moment: dust, body bounce, a thump. On dirt, default stability control halves, and the handbrake (rear lock, 28% side grip) is how you rotate in hairpins.\n\n### Cameras\n\nChase near (6.8 m back, 2.4 up), chase far (8.5, 3.1), bonnet (0, 1.05, 0.2 on the car). Cycle with Triangle or C. Look-ahead 8 m, look height 1.1. FOV 58, rising to 66 with speed. Position spring ~8/s. Low-pass the camera's yaw a little so slides read: the camera shouldn't be nailed to the car. Hold Circle or B for look back. Right stick or right-drag orbits around the car and springs back. Small shake on kerbs and impacts via `engine.shake`. Recipe C3.\n\n### Replays\n\nRecord every car at 30 Hz into Float32Arrays: x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, steer, rpm, throttle, gear, flags (brake, sliding, airborne, in pit). Playback interpolates. Replays never re-simulate.\n\n**The director:** per track, auto-place camera posts every ~280 m at 15 to 25 m off the road and 3 to 8 m up (tele, FOV 18 to 30, tracking), and add a few authored shots per track (start-line low, helicopter on the straight, bridge or gantry). Pick the next post ahead of the focus car, cut every 4 to 8 s, and when a battle or a slide happens prefer that car. Bars and a small `REPLAY` tag top-left.\n\n**Controls:** Cross play/pause, left/right scrub, L1/R1 change focus car, Triangle change camera mode (Director, Chase, Bonnet, Free), R2 hold slow motion ×0.25. Mouse: click a car to focus it, drag to orbit in Free, wheel to zoom. HUD hide toggle for a clean view.\n\n**Saving:** keep the last race in memory. `Save` writes a compressed copy (10 Hz, Int16 quantised, base64) to storage, 3 slots, and refuses politely if storage is full. Time trial's best lap is stored the same way as the ghost.\n\n---\n## 6. Content\n\nAll of this is data in `src/game/data/`. Physics rows for the cars and all track corners are in Appendix B.\n\n### World\n\nThe **Halcyon Peninsula**: a fictional stretch of coast, mountains and salt flats with a long, slightly eccentric love of motor cars. People here wash their cars on Sundays and argue about tyre pressures at weddings.\n\n### Marques and cars\n\n| Id | Car | Year | Layout | PS | kg | Price (CR) | Where |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| pico | Tsubame Pico 660 | 1991 | FF | 64 | 720 | 4,800 | Used lot |\n| kite | Tsubame Kite 1.6 RS | 1996 | FF | 148 | 1,040 | 12,500 | Used lot |\n| ginga | Kaminari Ginga S | 1994 | FR | 205 | 1,230 | 14,800 | Used lot |\n| moth | Castellan Moth 1.8 | 1998 | FR | 135 | 860 | 24,000 | Dealer |\n| ryu | Kaminari Ryu 2.0T | 1999 | 4WD turbo | 280 | 1,340 | 39,000 | Dealer |\n| longhorn | Ironwood Longhorn 428 | 1969 | FR | 420 | 1,610 | 47,000 | Dealer |\n| brandt32 | Brandt 3.2 CSR | 2000 | FR | 320 | 1,450 | 58,000 | Dealer |\n| heck | Brandt Heck 3.6 | 1997 | RR | 360 | 1,380 | 92,000 | Dealer |\n| libeccio | Vespucci Libeccio | 1995 | MR | 380 | 1,250 | 135,000 | Dealer |\n| kiteCup | Tsubame Kite Cup Racer | 2000 | FF | 210 | 930 | Prize | Featherweight Trophy |\n| ryuRally | Kaminari Ryu Rally Spec | 1999 | 4WD turbo | 330 | 1,230 | Prize | Red Clay Rally |\n| works | Kaminari Ginga Works GT | 2000 | FR | 560 | 1,180 | Prize, then 310,000 | Harbour Lights 200 |\n| corsa | Vespucci Libeccio Corsa | 1998 | MR | 620 | 1,100 | Prize, then 520,000 | Peninsula Touring Trophy |\n| type9 | Halcyon Type 9 Prototype | 2001 | MR | 780 | 930 | Prize only | The Halcyon Grand Prix |\n\nMarque personalities, for text and badges: **Tsubame** (small, clever, swallow badge), **Kaminari** (thunder; serious Japanese-flavoured performance), **Castellan** (English; a shed, a lathe, a principle), **Brandt** (German-flavoured engineering, polite and terrifying), **Ironwood** (American; displacement as a moral position), **Vespucci** (Italian-flavoured; beautiful, a little dramatic), **Halcyon Works** (the Peninsula's own tiny race shop).\n\nStarting credits: **15,000**. All three used cars are affordable, and buying the Kite or Ginga leaves very little: that is the point.\n\nSelling returns 50% of the price. You can't sell your last car, so no save can get stuck. Prize cars can't be sold: \"Prize cars are not for sale. It is simply not done.\"\n\n### Tyres\n\n| Tyre | `tyreMu` | `alphaP` | dirt, gravel factor | Wear × | Price |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Street | 0.95 | 0.14 | 0.45 | 0.8 | Fitted to Pico |\n| Sport | 1.00 | 0.125 | 0.50 | 1.0 | 1,200 |\n| Semi-slick | 1.12 | 0.115 | 0.42 | 1.4 | 4,800 |\n| Racing slick | 1.30 | 0.105 | 0.35 | 2.2 | 12,000 |\n| Rally dirt | 0.84 | 0.17 | 0.72 | 1.2 | 2,500 |\n\nAppendix B's car rows are the stock setups: a car keeps its own `tyreMu`, `alphaP` and `tyreTable` until the player buys tyres. `tyreTable` maps `dirt` and `gravel` to the factor; other surfaces use `SURFACES`. Wear × goes in `wearX`.\n\n### Parts\n\nEach one changes numbers in `tunedParams`. \"Slider\" means a setting becomes available on the Setup tab once bought. Each visible result is listed.\n\n| Category | Part | Effect | Price |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Engine | Sport exhaust | power ×1.04; louder, deeper engine sound and crackle on lift | 900 |\n| Engine | Intake and ECU | power ×1.06 | 1,800 |\n| Engine | Stage 1, 2, 3 (exclusive) | power ×1.10, ×1.20, ×1.35; `rpmPeak` +0, +200, +400; `redline` and `upshift` +0, +200, +500 | 3,000, 8,000, 20,000 |\n| Engine | Turbo kit 1, 2 (exclusive) | Turbo cars: power ×1.15, ×1.35. Others: ×1.25, ×1.50 and `turbo: true`, `turboLag: 0.8`; turbo whistle and blow-off appear | 6,000, 15,000 |\n| Weight | Stage 1, 2, 3 (exclusive) | mass ×0.95, ×0.90, ×0.85; `cgH` ×0.99, ×0.98, ×0.96 | 1,500, 4,500, 12,000 |\n| Drivetrain | Clutch and flywheel | `shiftTime` 0.11 | 1,200 |\n| Drivetrain | Race gearbox | `shiftTime` 0.08; slider: Gearing (`final` ×0.85 to ×1.15, labelled ACCELERATION to TOP SPEED) | 5,000 |\n| Drivetrain | Limited-slip diff | slider: LSD (`lsd` 0.2 to 0.8) | 2,500 |\n| Suspension | Sport | `loadK` 0.085, `cgH` ×0.96; slider: Balance (`rollF` 0.45 to 0.70, labelled TURNS IN to STABLE) | 2,000 |\n| Suspension | Race | `loadK` 0.07, `cgH` ×0.92; sliders: Balance, Ride height (`cgH` a further ×1.00 to ×0.90; below ×0.94 kerbs jolt the body) | 6,000 |\n| Brakes | Sport pads | `brakeG` +0.15 | 1,500 |\n| Brakes | Race kit | `brakeG` +0.40; slider: Balance (`brakeF` 0.50 to 0.75) | 5,000 |\n| Aero | Street kit | `clA` +0.15, `cdA` +0.02; a lip spoiler appears on the model | 2,500 |\n| Aero | Big wing | `clA` +0.50, `cdA` +0.06; slider: Downforce (×0.5 to ×1.5); a large wing appears on the model | 6,000 |\n| Tyres | see table | | |\n| Body | Paint (any of the 16 palette colours) | Model recolours, shown under showroom lights | 500 |\n| Body | Rims (4 styles) | Hub colour and spoke pattern change | 300 |\n\nDisplayed power and weight come from `tunedParams`. Event limits read those numbers. Engine sound follows `rpmPeak` and exhaust. Show a dyno pull (section 9) on buying any engine part: the before and after curve drawn in the HUD, with the engine sound rising.\n\n### Service Bay\n\n- **Oil change, 250 CR.** Each 40 km after the first 200 km since a change takes 0.5% of power, down to −8%. `c.oil` carries it. A fresh change gives a small bonus of +2% for the first 100 km. The mechanic says so in one line.\n- **Car wash, 50 CR.** No performance effect (\"It is simply polite.\"). Mud builds up on dirt (`dirt` 0..1 on the car) and the wash removes it: see section 8.\n\n### Licences\n\nEach test is data: `{ id, title, carId, track, startS, startSpeed, standing, end, limits, assists, medals, brief, tip, demo }`. `limits` says what fails the attempt (off the road, a stop outside the box, recovery). Times run from the first movement, or from the start line for rolling tests. Compute `medals` with `tools/medals.mjs`: run the AI demonstration in the sim at `skill: 0.97`, time T, then gold = T×1.03, silver = T×1.09, bronze = T×1.18, rounded to 0.01 s, and freeze the numbers in the data. A test passes at bronze. A licence is won when all four tests have at least bronze.\n\n`Cn` below is corner index n of that track's list (`tr.cornerS[n]` is its apex).\n\n**Licence C, \"Provisional\".** Car: Kite (stock, street tyres). Track: Proving Ground. Reward: 2,000 CR. All gold: the Pico as a prize.\n\n| Id | Title | Section | Lesson |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| C-1 | Start and Stop | Standing, 400 m along the long straight, stop inside a 30 m white box | The brake is a pedal with a far end |\n| C-2 | First Corner | Rolling 60 km/h, C0 −100 m to C1 +100 m | Turn in, apex, unwind |\n| C-3 | Cone Weave | Rolling 50 km/h down the straight through 6 cones at 40 m spacing. A hit cone adds 1 s | Weight moves |\n| C-4 | The Short Loop | C2 −50 m to C6 +50 m | Link corners, keep your head up |\n\n**Licence B, \"Club\".** Car: Ginga. Reward: 5,000 CR. All gold: Castellan Moth as a prize.\n\n| Id | Title | Section | Lesson |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| B-1 | Threshold | Proving straight, rolling 160 km/h, ABS off, stop inside a box 150 m on. Locking up is allowed and costs time | Squeeze, don't stamp |\n| B-2 | Hairpin Exit | Kestrel, C5 −150 m to C7 +60 m. Traction control 0 | Feed the throttle |\n| B-3 | Three Layouts | Proving C7 to C10, driven three times in Kite, Ginga, Ryu; times added | FF, FR, 4WD in the same corners |\n| B-4 | One Lap of Kestrel | Kestrel, flying lap | Rhythm |\n\n**Licence A, \"National\".** Reward: 10,000 CR. All gold: 25,000 CR and a gold helmet on the trophy shelf.\n\n| Id | Title | Car | Section | Lesson |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A-1 | Blind Crest | Brandt 3.2 | Cedar, C3 −100 m to C5 +100 m | Trust the road you remember |\n| A-2 | Switchbacks | Moth | Cedar, C7 to C10, uphill | Momentum |\n| A-3 | Red Clay | Ryu Rally | Red Clay, C7 to C10, dirt | Rotate with the handbrake |\n| A-4 | Harbour at Night | Libeccio | Harbour Lights, flying lap, no margin for error | Everything, by lamplight |\n\nAfter each attempt: medal, time, gap to the next medal, then **Retry**, **Watch your replay**, **Demonstration** (the AI drives it, label `DEMONSTRATION`, examiner's voice over), **Back**. Three failures in a row: the examiner offers the Driving line for this test.\n\n### Events\n\nPoints per round: 10, 8, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1. Most points wins the series. Prize money is paid every round to the top four in the ratio 100%, 60%, 40%, 20%. The Bonus and prize car come only from winning the series. Each race advances the day counter.\n\n| Id | Event | Needs | Restriction | Rounds (track, laps) | AI pace | AI pool | 1st prize | Bonus |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| dawn | Dawn Patrol Cup | C | ≤210 PS | Kestrel 2; Harbour at dusk 2; Kestrel 3 | .86–.90 | Pico, Kite, Moth | 1,500 | 3,000 |\n| fellow | Front-Drive Fellowship | C | FF, ≤230 PS | Cedar 2; Saltline 4 | .88–.91 | Kite, Kite (tuned), Pico (tuned) | 2,000 | 5,000 |\n| feather | Featherweight Trophy | B | ≤1,100 kg | Cedar 3; Kestrel 3; Harbour at dusk 3 | .90–.93 | Moth, Kite Cup, Pico (tuned) | 3,000 | 8,000 + Kite Cup Racer |\n| society | Rear-Drive Society | B | FR | Kestrel in rain 3; Saltline 5 | .91–.94 | Ginga, Brandt 3.2, Longhorn | 3,500 | 10,000 |\n| clay | Red Clay Rally | B | Any; dirt tyres advised | Red Clay, 2 laps, 3 legs against one rival each | .91–.95 | Ryu, Ryu Rally | 4,000 | Ryu Rally Spec |\n| touring | Peninsula Touring Trophy | A | ≤520 PS | Cedar 3; Harbour at night 3; Saltline 6; Kestrel 4 | .93–.96 | Brandt 3.2, Heck, Libeccio, Longhorn, Ryu (tuned) | 6,000 | 40,000 + Libeccio Corsa |\n| h200 | Harbour Lights 200 | A | Any | Harbour, 10 laps, dusk into night, one stop needed, field of 8 | .92–.95 | Heck, Libeccio, Brandt 3.2 (tuned) | 20,000 | Ginga Works GT |\n| gp | The Halcyon Grand Prix | A and Touring or H200 won | Any | Kestrel 5; Cedar 5; Saltline 8; Harbour at night 5 | .96–.99 | Works, Corsa, Libeccio (tuned) | 30,000 | Type 9, ending |\n\nTwenty-two races and twelve tests is about three hours for a new player. The ten-lap endurance needs exactly one stop at default rates: in testing, tyres fall to zero by lap 9 and the tank empties on lap 9 or 10, and lap time drifts from 117 s to 135 s. Short races use `wearRate` ×0.5.\n\n**Winning the GP:** a podium scene, the Type 9 reveal, then the credits, then the ending card, in the catalogue voice: \"You may keep driving. Most people do.\"\n\n### Arcade\n\nThe Arcade Gate on the map skips the career: **Quick Race** (any track, any car, laps, field size, Easy .85 / Normal .92 / Hard .98, hour, rain), **Time Trial** (any track and car, ghost of your best), **Couch Duel** (section 14). Every car and track is open here from the first minute, so someone trying the demo can see everything quickly. It pays no credits.\n\n### Home Garage and Museum\n\n**Home Garage:** your cars on a turntable with mileage, oil, wear and setup; choose your ride; sell; a trophy shelf with a 3D cup or medal for every win; your stats (days, km, wins, gold medals, % collected).\n\n**Museum:** all 14 cars with their brochure text and silhouette (unowned cars show as a dark silhouette until seen in a race), plus a page per track: map, length, corners, records.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Screens and controls\n","numLines":285,"startLine":100,"totalLines":1331}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Koz5whSoeGzDGYFwGZZPN3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
