{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkiJqToKHCVmeZ5T8vLS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WSBnqNvhsfyBnobcwz1ehY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261105-162057__x4c6ec5/work/_research && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    s=open(path,encoding='utf8').read()\n    for a,b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, a[:70]\n        s=s.replace(a,b)\n    open(path,'w',encoding='utf8').write(s)\npatch('plan_part1.md',[\n(\"Very well. Cars 8.5 m ahead are about 70 art pixels wide and instantly readable\",\"Very well. A car seen from the chase camera is about 40 art pixels wide and instantly readable, and kerbs, banking and night lighting all hold up\"),\n(\"`loadGame` frees music, sets and lights. Keep all menus\",\"`loadGame` frees the scene's objects, the music and the lights. Keep all menus\"),\n(\"work and look right. Use fewer, thinner drops than the default near the camera |\",\"work and look right. Drops close to the camera look large: keep `count` modest and the `area` wide |\"),\n(\"### Engine facts that will otherwise cost you hours\",\"**Not proven.** No human has driven these cars, and there was no real pad, TV or listener here, only AI and scripted drivers. Treat the handling as a strong start and tune the feel yourself (steering rate, response curve, camera) in build step 3. Medal times, prizes and AI pace ranges are first estimates; your whole-game bot and play-testing should adjust them. The menus, engine sound, voices, music, pit stop and replay director are designed here but weren't prototyped.\\n\\n### Engine facts that will otherwise cost you hours\"),\n])\npatch('plan_part2.md',[\n(\"| works | Kaminari Ginga Works GT | 2000 | FR | 560 | 1,180 | Prize, then 310,000 | Harbour Lights 200 |\",\"| works | Kaminari Ginga Works GT | 2000 | FR | 560 | 1,180 | Prize, or 310,000 after Licence A | Harbour Lights 200 |\"),\n(\"| corsa | Vespucci Libeccio Corsa | 1998 | MR | 620 | 1,100 | Prize, then 520,000 | Peninsula Touring Trophy |\",\"| corsa | Vespucci Libeccio Corsa | 1998 | MR | 620 | 1,100 | Prize, or 520,000 after Licence A | Peninsula Touring Trophy |\"),\n(\"| Street | 0.95 | 0.14 | 0.45 | 0.8 | Fitted to Pico |\",\"| Street | 0.95 | 0.14 | 0.45 | 0.8 | 600 (close to stock on Pico and Kite) |\"),\n(\"Node has no context: guard it, and count `engine` plays through `audio.counts` for tests.\",\"Node has no context: guard it, and let tests read the synth's last rpm and throttle.\"),\n(\"| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §17, below |\",\"| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §17, below |\\n| Effort as you see fit | §17 sets the order and what may shrink |\\n| This computer: pad stubs, touch profiles, Web Audio checks, 1080p screenshots | §16 |\"),\n(\"**Second**, multiplayer also exists without the hub, on one screen:\\n\\n**Couch Duel** (Arcade Gate): two players, one TV, split screen, any track and car, with optional AI cars and real contact. Implementation (tested):\",\"**Second**, multiplayer also exists without the hub, on one screen:\\n\\n**Couch Duel** (Arcade Gate): two players, one TV, split screen, any track and car, with optional AI cars and real contact. Implementation (the two-engine pattern with a shared plain-JS state is tested):\"),\n])\np='tools/assemble.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"parts = ''.join(open(os.path.join(root, f'plan_part{i}.md'), encoding='utf8').read() for i in (1, 2, 3))\",\"parts = '\\\\n'.join(open(os.path.join(root, f'plan_part{i}.md'), encoding='utf8').read() for i in (1, 2, 3))\")\ns=s.replace(\"import re, sys, os\",\"import sys, os\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 tools/assemble.py ../PLAN.md; cd .. ; grep -n \"^---$\" -A1 PLAN.md | grep -c \"^[0-9]*-## \"; grep -n \"—\" PLAN.md | head -3; grep -c \"\" PLAN.md; rm -rf _research/final/game.html; cd _research && mkdir -p final2 && rm -rf final/src/game/sim final/src/